    # the code is this phase's. What differs, and why:
    #  QA. The phase, the log directory and the subjects are M4 part 1 P2's:
    #      the base M4 part 1 P1's record commit, then the doc commit and the
    #      six code commits, the last (prefix_len) the phase commit, each by
    #      its full subject. The spec is specs/0030, pinned at its blob at the
    #      doc commit, 31cd9689 (FACTS.md); the working file, planning's
    #      rulings during P2, is printed and not asserted. The status pattern
    #      allows this phase's logs and planning's uncommitted specs/0030 alone.
    #  QB. This log builds: cargo test, clippy and doc in <repo> into
    #      <target>/main, the phase's one target root (specs/0001), serially;
    #      no fixture, no binary copied, no corpus.
    #  QC. <scratch>/w holds the captured cargo outputs, the two trees
    #      extracted by git archive and the controls' fixtures, kept on the
    #      disk under <build>; this script removes no directory.
    #  QD. Root lines for the placeholders the carried history prints before a
    #      slash and this log never uses, each saying so.
    #
    # P1's text:
    # Milestone 4 part 1 P1 test.log
    # (specs/0030-carries-and-api-changes.md, "### P1": "The test log: the
    # script on a fixture run directory with and without a planted error row,
    # the counts shown"; item 1; decision 1 A and "Planning rulings during P1"
    # rulings 2 and 6). The phase commit's scripts/excel-check-list.py and
    # scripts/passthrough-run.sh, over FICTIONAL fixtures this script builds in
    # <scratch>/w/fx (no corpus file is read; nothing runs in <repo>):
    #
    #   T1 the list, --run root1/runs/run-formula --run-plain
    #      root1/runs/run-plain, no error row: exit 0, the counts line, stderr
    #      EMPTY (ruling 6: no note for a directory with none), the list with
    #      mode 600, its rows counted by source.
    #   T2 the same with run-plain copied to run-plain-planted and one error row
    #      planted there (fx-b: outcome error, out_bytes empty, its output
    #      removed, as the runner leaves it): exit 0, stderr exactly one line,
    #      the note for 1 row of run-plain-planted (built from the source's
    #      own form), one corpus row fewer than T1, fx-b absent under that
    #      label.
    #   T2b the planted row in the --run directory instead (run-formula copied
    #      to run-formula-planted): the note names "host".
    #   T3 the runner, the clone's scripts/passthrough-run.sh at the phase
    #      commit, over the fixture corpus root rroot with the gate's DEBUG
    #      emend-copy and xlsx-diff copied, no --libreoffice, --ids selecting
    #      fa0000000001:
    #      T3a a fresh run directory: exit 0, one ok row;
    #      T3b a fresh run directory with fa0000000001/lo.host planted: exit 2,
    #          the earlier-run message from the source, no row, no output, the
    #          planted directory still there;
    #      T3c the same with lo-in.host;
    #      T3d only fa0000000001/lo.i686 planted, --label host: not refused,
    #          one ok row, lo.i686 left in place;
    #      T3e lo.host planted under fa0000000002, which --ids does not select:
    #          refused (every subdirectory counts, ruling 2).
    #   Every message and the note's form are read from the sources by grep,
    #   never typed; each pass check has a control that refuses another case's
    #   output.
    #
    # CARRIED TO M4 part 1 P1 from M3 part 7 P4's test script (printed in
    # records/logs/m3p7-p4/test.log), generated by
    # <home>/.cache/emend-build/m4p1-p1/gen/test.py with gen/p1_common.py.
    # P4's cases (the carried close-out scripts and their generator) are P4's
    # and are not rerun. P4's comment text follows below as the carried history;
    # the code is this phase's. What differs, and why:
    #  KA. The phase, the log directory and the subjects are M4 part 1 P1's: the
    #      base M3 part 7's close-out record commit, then the doc commit, the
    #      rules commit (specs/0001), the runner commit and the list commit,
    #      the phase commit, each by its full subject. The spec is specs/0030,
    #      pinned at its blob at the doc commit, 7bc47cae (FACTS.md); the
    #      working file, planning's rulings during P1, is printed and not
    #      asserted. The status pattern allows this phase's logs and
    #      planning's uncommitted specs/0030 alone.
    #  KB. No build. scripts/counting.sh and scripts/excel-check-list.py are
    #      read at the phase commit by git show into <scratch>/w; the runner is
    #      run from a clone of <repo> at the phase commit in <scratch>/w/clone
    #      (the runner finds its repository as its own directory's parent and
    #      reads its commit, Cargo.lock and rustc there, and sources
    #      scripts/lo-check.sh beside it); the gate's DEBUG emend-copy and
    #      xlsx-diff are copied from <target>/main/debug into <scratch>/w/bin
    #      and each copy's sha256 checked against the one line gate.log
    #      printed for it.
    #  KC. The fixtures, built under <scratch>/w/fx by a python3 -I program this
    #      script writes beside them (printed), all fictional. <scratch>/w, with
    #      the fixtures, the clone and the cases' outputs, is kept on the disk
    #      under <build>; this script removes no directory.
    #  KD. Root lines for the placeholders the carried history prints before a
    #      slash and this log never uses, each saying so.
    #
    # P4's text:
    # Milestone 3 part 7 P4 test.log (specs/0029-engineering-close.md, "P4:
    # the README and the list" as amended 2026-10-09, "The Excel check",
    # "Close-out push (after P4)" as amended, and "Planning rulings during P4
    # (2026-10-09)" rulings 3 and 4): the spec pinned by the hash of its
    # committed blob, planning's working copy printed; the phase's three
    # commits by role; T1 part 6's close-out push, ci-run and scan scripts,
    # copied to <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-close/carried, each equal to the
    # text part 6's committed logs printed; T2 the counting library the
    # close-out sources, equal to the phase commit's scripts/counting.sh, and
    # its one line of difference from part 6's copy, which part 6's push.log
    # printed; T3 gen.py printed and run into a scratch directory, the three
    # scripts it writes equal to the ones on the disk; T4 each generated
    # script's diff against part 6's, printed in full; T5 bash -n, the three
    # shape greps with fixtures, and no non-ASCII byte, U+2014 or home path in
    # each generated script; T6 the Excel-record check's three functions and
    # its pre-mode section present once each, the base, record and tip
    # patterns resolved or read; this log runs no cargo; this script's own
    # stderr counted.
    #
    #
    # Usage: m5p6-p4-test.sh <phase commit> > <file outside the tree>; the
    # caller moves the output to records/logs/m5p6-p4/test.log.
    set -uo pipefail
    SELF_DIR=$(cd "$(dirname "$0")" && pwd)
    SELF=$SELF_DIR/$(basename "$0")
    # specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7: this script's own standard error, kept and counted at the end.
    mkdir -p "$SELF_DIR/out" || exit 2
    ERR=$SELF_DIR/out/test.stderr
    exec 2>"$ERR"
    cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 2
    MAIN=$(pwd)
    
    C=${1:?phase commit required}
    unset EMEND_CORPUS_DIR EMEND_KEEP_DIR RUSTDOCFLAGS RUSTFLAGS CARGO_TARGET_DIR
    export RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0 CARGO_TERM_COLOR=never
    PHASE_DIR=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m6p3-p3
    BUILD_ROOT=${TEST_BUILD:-$PHASE_DIR/test}
    SUPERSEDED_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/superseded
    TARGET_DIR=$PHASE_DIR/target
    SPEC=specs/0040-analytic-chart-elements.md
    SPEC_WANT=a02a208982fd79027a27988a409b1ad85e1b457c66b4f662cc5f3964a8b6af8e
    # Change WS (M6 part 2 P3's change VZ): where T1 writes the listing and
    # where R2 installs the record; a dry run names stand-ins outside the
    # repository.
    API_DIR=${TEST_API_DIR:-$PHASE_DIR/api}
    RECORDS_DEST=${TEST_RECORDS_DEST:-records}
    mkdir -p "$BUILD_ROOT" || exit 2
    # Change QC: made on the disk under <build> and kept after the run.
    B=$(mktemp -d -p "$BUILD_ROOT") || exit 2
    git show "$C:scripts/counting.sh" >"$B/counting.sh" || exit 2
    . "$B/counting.sh"
    fail=0
    check() { echo "  $1: $2"; [ "$2" = yes ] || fail=1; }
    yn() { if "$@"; then echo yes; else echo no; fi; }
    # For a condition that must NOT hold: a leading bang inside yn runs a
    # command named by the bang (specs/0001), so a negation has its own helper.
    ynnot() { if "$@"; then echo no; else echo yes; fi; }
    
    head_is() { [ "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" = "$1" ]; }
    full_sha() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9a-f]{40}$'; }
    # The given commit is the phase commit when it is a full sha and HEAD.
    given_ok() { full_sha "$1" && head_is "$1"; }
    if given_ok "$C"; then :; else echo "the phase commit must be a full 40-hex sha that is HEAD, not $C" >&2; exit 2; fi
    NULL_SHA=0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
    case "${C: -1}" in 0) LAST=1 ;; *) LAST=0 ;; esac
    FAKE_SHA=${C:0:39}$LAST
    SHORT_SHA=${C:0:7}
    # This phase's logs, untracked, and the API record this log writes, the
    # phase commit's short sha (changes RA, UA, UI, UR, UY, VG, VJ, VN, WB, WE,
    # WH, WP and WS). Change WW (ruling S): OWN is the phase's own paths, the
    # pattern the status labels count; OURS adds planning's working spec when
    # admitted, the pattern the accounted checks read.
    OURS="^(\\?\\? records/logs/m6p3-p3/|\\?\\? records/api-review-m6p3-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-${SHORT_SHA}[.]md\$)"
    OWN=$OURS
    PLAN_LINE="^ M specs/0040-analytic-chart-elements[.]md\$"
    
    # Change VM (kept, with WB's names): planning's working copy of the
    # spec (its rulings during the phase, uncommitted until the record commit)
    # is admitted, modified, when PLANNING_SPEC is given and the working file
    # hashes to it; otherwise the pattern is WB's.
    PLAN_SPEC_NOW=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    plan_admitted() { [ -n "${PLANNING_SPEC:-}" ] && [ "$PLAN_SPEC_NOW" = "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; }
    if plan_admitted; then OURS="^(\\?\\? records/logs/m6p3-p3/|\\?\\? records/api-review-m6p3-[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}-${SHORT_SHA}[.]md\$| M specs/0040-analytic-chart-elements[.]md\$)"; fi
    entry_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    entry_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    entry_own=$(run_matches -E "$OWN" git status --porcelain)
    entry_plan=$(run_matches -E "$PLAN_LINE" git status --porcelain)
    entry_clean() { [ "$entry_all" != error ] && [ "$entry_ours" != error ] && [ "$entry_all" = "$entry_ours" ]; }
    if entry_clean; then :; else
      echo "the working tree holds changes outside this phase's logs and its API record" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    
    scrub() {
      sed -e "s#$MAIN#<repo>#g" -e "s#$SELF_DIR#<scripts>#g" -e "s#$B#<scratch>/w#g" \
        -e "s#$BUILD_ROOT#<build>#g" -e "s#$SUPERSEDED_DIR#<superseded>#g" \
        -e "s#$TARGET_DIR#<target>#g" -e "s#$API_DIR#<api>#g" -e "s#$PHASE_DIR#<phase>#g" \
        -e "s#$HOME#<home>#g"
    }
    exec 3>&1
    exec > >(scrub >&3)
    SCRUB_PID=$!
    
    echo "command: git rev-parse HEAD"
    echo "invocation: bash <scripts>/$(basename "$0") $*"
    echo "input: RERUN_NOTE: ${RERUN_NOTE:-unset}"
    echo "input: RERUN_FILES: ${RERUN_FILES:-unset}"
    echo "input: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo set || echo unset) (its value never printed)"
    echo "input: HOME: set, read for the paths under it, printed as <home>"
    echo "input: TEST_BUILD: ${TEST_BUILD:-unset} (the build root, <build>)"
    echo "input: TEST_API_DIR: ${TEST_API_DIR:-unset} (the listing's directory, <api>; the default <phase>/api: $([ "$API_DIR" = "$PHASE_DIR/api" ] && echo yes || echo no); change WS)"
    echo "input: TEST_RECORDS_DEST: ${TEST_RECORDS_DEST:-unset} (the records' destination: $RECORDS_DEST; the default records, in <repo>: $([ "$RECORDS_DEST" = records ] && echo yes || echo no); change WS)"
    echo "input: PLANNING_SPEC: ${PLANNING_SPEC:-unset} (planning's working copy's hash; the working file admitted modified at it: $(yn plan_admitted); change VM)"
    echo "input: RUSTDOCFLAGS, RUSTFLAGS and CARGO_TARGET_DIR: unset by this script at entry; each cargo command below names its target directory"
    echo "about: M6 part 3 P3 phase commit $C; HEAD at run: $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo
    echo "## the shape greps, the three and PYB, and the defined-helper check, over this script, before its log (specs/0001; ruling Z; change UF)"
    D='$'
    SHAPE_CHAIN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) .*(&&|\\|\\|)"
    SHAPE_BANG="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) !"
    SHAPE_ASSIGN="\\${D}\\((yn|ynnot|is|isnot) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*="
    printf '%s\n' "x=${D}(is [ 1 ] && true)" "y=${D}(isnot ! true)" "z=${D}(yn N=1 true)" >"$B/shape-fixture"
    echo "command: count_matches -E <shape> <this script>, and the same over a fixture holding one line of each shape"
    for shape in CHAIN BANG ASSIGN; do
      var=SHAPE_$shape
      n_self=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$SELF")
      n_fix=$(count_matches -E "${!var}" "$B/shape-fixture")
      echo "  shape $shape: in this script $n_self; in the fixture $n_fix"
      check "$shape: this script holds none" "$(yn [ "$n_self" = 0 ])"
      check "control: $shape: the same form finds the fixture's one line" "$(yn [ "$n_fix" = 1 ])"
    done
    # Change UF: the fourth shape, PYB, M5 part 6's form: a line that is not a comment
    # and calls python3 (followed by whitespace, then a dash or a .py path)
    # without -I -B. The interpreter's name is held in a variable here, so no
    # line of this form spells a call.
    PY=python3
    PYB_CALL="^[^#]*$PY[[:space:]]+(-|[^[:space:]]*[.]py)"
    PYB_OK="$PY -I -B( |\$)"
    # pyb_calls <file> and pyb_without <file>: the calls, and the calls without
    # -I -B. They print, so their values are compared.
    pyb_calls() { count_matches -E "$PYB_CALL" "$1"; }
    pyb_without() { LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "$PYB_CALL" "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -vE "$PYB_OK" | count_lines /dev/stdin; }
    printf '%s\n' "$PY -c x" "$PY -I -B -c x" "# $PY -c x" "command -v $PY" >"$B/shape-pyb-fixture"
    n_pyb_self=$(pyb_without "$SELF")
    n_pyb_fix=$(pyb_without "$B/shape-pyb-fixture")
    n_calls_self=$(pyb_calls "$SELF")
    n_calls_fix=$(pyb_calls "$B/shape-pyb-fixture")
    echo "  shape PYB: in this script $n_pyb_self (of its $n_calls_self Python calls); in the fixture $n_pyb_fix (of its $n_calls_fix)"
    check "PYB: this script holds none (change UF)" "$(yn [ "$n_pyb_self" = 0 ])"
    check "control: PYB: the same form finds the fixture's one call without -I -B, of its two calls, the comment and the command -v line not calls" "$(yn [ "$n_pyb_fix:$n_calls_fix" = 1:2 ])"
    check "control: the call form finds this script's 10 Python call lines, the defined-helper check's two runs, the listing program's two, the formatter's one, and their five command lines (changes UF, VJ, WE and WS)" "$(yn [ "$n_calls_self" = 10 ])"
    check "control: ynnot reports no on a passing command" "$(yn [ "$(ynnot true)" = no ])"
    # Change UF (ruling Z): the defined-helper check over this script's own
    # source, by the phase's gen/defined.py copied into <scratch>/w and checked
    # by its sha256, then over a planted script, the control.
    DEF_WANT=ee9f81359e07025bf08825c9562a853c3403115dc9a4f39c554f90533df9ca6d
    cp "$PHASE_DIR/gen/defined.py" "$B/defined.py" </dev/null
    def_cp_rc=$?
    DEF_HAVE=$(sha256sum <"$B/defined.py" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: cp <phase>/gen/defined.py <scratch>/w/defined.py: exit $def_cp_rc; sha256sum: $DEF_HAVE"
    def_copied() { [ "$def_cp_rc" = 0 ] && [ "$DEF_HAVE" = "$DEF_WANT" ]; }
    check "the copy is the defined-helper program this script was generated against, sha256 $DEF_WANT (changes UF and UO)" "$(yn def_copied)"
    echo "command: sed 's/^/    /' <scratch>/w/defined.py"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/defined.py"
    DEF_RUN='import importlib.util, sys; s = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location("defined", sys.argv[1]); d = importlib.util.module_from_spec(s); s.loader.exec_module(d); d.check(open(sys.argv[2]).read(), sys.argv[3])'
    echo "command: python3 -I -B -c <the loader: the program loaded from its path, its check run over the file> <scratch>/w/defined.py <this script> $(basename "$SELF")"
    python3 -I -B -c "$DEF_RUN" "$B/defined.py" "$SELF" "$(basename "$SELF")" >"$B/defined-self.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    def_rc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/defined-self.out"
    echo "  exit $def_rc"
    def_self_ok() { [ "$def_rc" = 0 ] && [ "$(count_lines "$B/defined-self.out")" = 5 ] && [ "$(count_matches -E ': yes$' "$B/defined-self.out")" = 5 ]; }
    check "every helper a yn, ynnot, is or isnot call of this script names is defined in it, the four themselves where it calls them are defined in it, and the program's three planted controls find their planted names (5 lines yes; rulings Z, AD and AK a; changes UF and UO)" "$(yn def_self_ok)"
    # The planted calls are built from pieces, so this text holds no call of an
    # undefined name.
    printf '%s\n' 'f() { :; }' "x=\$""(yn f)" "y=\$""(ynnot g)" >"$B/c-defined.sh"
    echo "command: python3 -I -B -c <the loader> <scratch>/w/defined.py <scratch>/w/c-defined.sh c-defined.sh (a planted script defining f and calling f and g)"
    python3 -I -B -c "$DEF_RUN" "$B/defined.py" "$B/c-defined.sh" c-defined.sh >"$B/c-defined.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    cdef_rc=$?
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/c-defined.out"
    echo "  exit $cdef_rc"
    def_ctl_ok() { [ "$cdef_rc" != 0 ] && [ "$(count_matches -F 'no, undefined: g' "$B/c-defined.out")" = 1 ]; }
    check "control: the same program names g undefined in the planted script and exits non-zero (ruling Z; change UF)" "$(yn def_ctl_ok)"
    # Change UV (ruling D): this script's own placeholder check, the scan's rule.
    # placeholders_used <file>: every lower-case token printed before a slash,
    # and every scrub target, one per line, sorted and unique.
    TOK='<[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*>'
    placeholders_used() {
      {
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E "s#[^#]*#$TOK" "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E "$TOK\$"
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E "$TOK/" "$1" | sed 's#/$##'
      } | LC_ALL=C sort -u
    }
    # placeholders_declared <file>: the tokens a root line says stand for
    # something.
    placeholders_declared() {
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '(^|echo ")root: ' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E "$TOK(/[a-z0-9]+)? stands for" |
        LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -o -E "^$TOK" | LC_ALL=C sort -u
    }
    # undeclared <file>: the count of tokens used and not declared. It prints, so
    # its value is compared.
    undeclared() { LC_ALL=C comm -23 <(placeholders_used "$1") <(placeholders_declared "$1") | count_lines /dev/stdin; }
    echo "command: the scan's placeholder rule over this script: the tokens before a slash and the scrub targets, against the tokens its root lines declare"
    ph_used=$(placeholders_used "$SELF" | tr '\n' ' ')
    ph_decl=$(placeholders_declared "$SELF" | tr '\n' ' ')
    n_undecl=$(undeclared "$SELF")
    echo "  placeholders printed: $ph_used; declared by root lines: $ph_decl; undeclared: $n_undecl"
    check "every placeholder this script prints is declared by a root line (ruling D; change UV)" "$(yn [ "$n_undecl" = 0 ])"
    # The planted tokens are built from pieces, so this source spells none.
    L='<'
    printf 'root: %srepo> stands for x\nread %srepo>/a and %sbld>/b\n' "$L" "$L" "$L" >"$B/c-ph-bad"
    printf 'root: %srepo> stands for x; %sbld> stands for y\nread %srepo>/a and %sbld>/b\n' "$L" "$L" "$L" "$L" >"$B/c-ph-ok"
    printf '  sed -e "s#$X#%sgbld>#g"\nroot: %srepo> stands for x\n' "$L" "$L" >"$B/c-ph-scrub"
    check "control: the same rule finds one undeclared token before a slash in a planted file (ruling D; change UV)" "$(yn [ "$(undeclared "$B/c-ph-bad")" = 1 ])"
    check "control: the same rule finds none when a root line declares it" "$(yn [ "$(undeclared "$B/c-ph-ok")" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same rule finds an undeclared scrub target" "$(yn [ "$(undeclared "$B/c-ph-scrub")" = 1 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## the phase's commits by role, read from git"
    by_subject() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1"; }
    REC=$(by_subject "M6 part 3 P2 record: the logs, the records, the check, the scan")
    DOC=$(by_subject "M6 part 3 P3: commit planning docs (the P2 verification and rulings)")
    CARRY=$(by_subject "M6 part 3 P3: the axis sample's module doc names the column's series without categories (ruling Q)")
    PROBE=$(by_subject "M6 part 3 P3: probe-emend-charts-write-xml gains the trendlines, error bars, plot lines and axis options")
    CHANGELOG=$(by_subject "M6 part 3 P3: the CHANGELOG names the analytic chart elements")
    PROBE2=$(by_subject "M6 part 3 P3: the 3D line's category axis takes the skips (ruling T)")
    echo "command: git log --format=%H -n 1 -F --grep=<the role's full subject>, for each role"
    echo "  the previous phase's record commit (the base, P2's record): ${REC:-none}"
    echo "  the doc commit: ${DOC:-none}"
    echo "  the carry commit (the axis sample's module doc, ruling Q): ${CARRY:-none}"
    echo "  the probe commit (probe-emend-charts-write-xml gains the trendlines, error bars, plot lines and axis options): ${PROBE:-none}"
    echo "  the CHANGELOG commit: ${CHANGELOG:-none}"
    echo "  the second probe commit (the 3D line's category axis takes the skips, ruling T), the phase commit: ${PROBE2:-none}"
    echo "command: git rev-parse <phase commit>~0 to <phase commit>~5"
    for k in 0 1 2 3 4 5; do git rev-parse "$C~$k"; done | sed 's/^/    /'
    roles_in_order() {
      local r k=0
      for r in "$PROBE2" "$CHANGELOG" "$PROBE" "$CARRY" "$DOC" "$REC"; do
        [ -n "$r" ] || return 1
        [ "$(git rev-parse "$C~$k")" = "$r" ] || return 1
        k=$((k + 1))
      done
    }
    check "the second probe commit, the CHANGELOG commit, the probe commit, the carry commit, the doc commit and the base, each the next one's parent, the second probe commit the phase commit (change WP)" "$(yn roles_in_order)"
    roles_ctl() { local PROBE2=$CHANGELOG; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the CHANGELOG commit named as the phase commit (change WP)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl)"
    roles_ctl4() { local CHANGELOG=$PROBE; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the probe commit named as the CHANGELOG commit (change WP)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl4)"
    roles_ctl2() { local DOC=$REC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the base named as the doc commit" "$(ynnot roles_ctl2)"
    roles_ctl3() { local CARRY=$DOC; roles_in_order; }
    check "control: roles_in_order refuses the doc commit named as the carry commit (change WP)" "$(ynnot roles_ctl3)"
    # Change WP: the files each commit changes; no crate source, no test file
    # and neither ops script among them.
    files_of() { git diff --name-only "$1" "$2" | paste -sd' ' -; }
    echo "command: git diff --name-only <each role's parent> <role>"
    echo "  the doc commit: $(files_of "$REC" "$DOC")"
    echo "  the carry commit: $(files_of "$DOC" "$CARRY")"
    echo "  the probe commit: $(files_of "$CARRY" "$PROBE")"
    echo "  the CHANGELOG commit: $(files_of "$PROBE" "$CHANGELOG")"
    echo "  the second probe commit: $(files_of "$CHANGELOG" "$PROBE2")"
    roles_files() {
      [ "$(files_of "$REC" "$DOC")" = "ROADMAP.md $SPEC" ] &&
        [ "$(files_of "$DOC" "$CARRY")" = "tools/emend-copy/src/main.rs" ] &&
        [ "$(files_of "$CARRY" "$PROBE")" = "tools/size-probe/src/bin/probe-emend-charts-write-xml.rs" ] &&
        [ "$(files_of "$PROBE" "$CHANGELOG")" = "CHANGELOG.md" ] &&
        [ "$(files_of "$CHANGELOG" "$PROBE2")" = "tools/size-probe/src/bin/probe-emend-charts-write-xml.rs" ]
    }
    check "each commit changes its own file or files alone: the doc commit planning's two, the carry commit the tool's main.rs, each probe commit the charts probe, the CHANGELOG commit CHANGELOG.md (change WP)" "$(yn roles_files)"
    roles_files_ctl() { local PROBE=$CARRY; roles_files; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the carry commit named as the probe commit (change WP)" "$(ynnot roles_files_ctl)"
    roles_files_ctl2() { local CHANGELOG=$PROBE; roles_files; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the probe commit named as the CHANGELOG commit (change WP)" "$(ynnot roles_files_ctl2)"
    roles_files_ctl3() { local PROBE2=$CHANGELOG; roles_files; }
    check "control: the same check refuses the CHANGELOG commit named as the second probe commit (change WP)" "$(ynnot roles_files_ctl3)"
    echo
    echo "phase: Milestone 6 part 3 P3 ($SPEC) test.log; run at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    # Ruling AK b (change UP): the hashing asserted, the run log's form, and
    # each named file under <superseded> (ruling AA).
    n_rerun_files=0
    n_rerun_missing=0
    n_rerun_outside=0
    # under_superseded <path>: the path lies inside <superseded>.
    under_superseded() { case "$1" in "$SUPERSEDED_DIR"/*) return 0 ;; esac; return 1; }
    # rerun_hashed: RERUN_FILES named at least one file, each there and each
    # under <superseded>.
    rerun_hashed() { [ "$n_rerun_files" -gt 0 ] && [ "$n_rerun_missing" = 0 ] && [ "$n_rerun_outside" = 0 ]; }
    # names_script <list>: one of the list's paths is a .sh file under
    # <superseded> (ruling F; change UW).
    names_script() {
      local f
      for f in $1; do
        case "$f" in "$SUPERSEDED_DIR"/*.sh) return 0 ;; esac
      done
      return 1
    }
    if [ -n "${RERUN_NOTE:-}" ]; then
      echo "rerun: $RERUN_NOTE"
      echo "command: sha256sum and wc -c over each superseded attempt named above, with the directory it is kept in (ruling AA; change UG)"
      for sf in ${RERUN_FILES:-}; do
        n_rerun_files=$((n_rerun_files + 1))
        under_superseded "$sf" || n_rerun_outside=$((n_rerun_outside + 1))
        if [ -f "$sf" ]; then
          printf '    %s  %s bytes  %s  kept in %s\n' "$(sha256sum "$sf" | cut -d' ' -f1)" "$(wc -c <"$sf")" "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        else
          n_rerun_missing=$((n_rerun_missing + 1))
          printf '    NO HASH EXISTS for %s: the file is not there at run time (named in %s)\n' "$(basename "$sf")" "$(dirname "$sf")"
        fi
      done
      if [ -z "${RERUN_FILES:-}" ]; then echo "    RERUN_FILES was not set, so no attempt above is hashed by this run"; fi
      echo "  files named $n_rerun_files; not there $n_rerun_missing; outside <superseded> $n_rerun_outside"
      check "every file of the attempt RERUN_NOTE names is hashed above, RERUN_FILES names at least one, and each lies in <superseded> (rulings AA and AK b; change UP)" "$(yn rerun_hashed)"
      check "RERUN_FILES names the superseded script that wrote the attempt, a .sh file under <superseded> (ruling F; change UW)" "$(yn names_script "${RERUN_FILES:-}")"
    fi
    rerun_ctl() { local n_rerun_files=1 n_rerun_missing=1 n_rerun_outside=0; rerun_hashed; }
    check "control: names_script refuses a list naming a log and its stderr alone (ruling F; change UW)" "$(ynnot names_script "$SUPERSEDED_DIR/a/test.log $SUPERSEDED_DIR/a/test.outer.stderr")"
    check "control: names_script refuses a script outside <superseded> (change UW)" "$(ynnot names_script "$PHASE_DIR/scripts/m6p3-p3-test.sh")"
    check "control: names_script takes a list naming a script under <superseded> (change UW)" "$(yn names_script "$SUPERSEDED_DIR/a/test.log $SUPERSEDED_DIR/a/m6p3-p3-test.sh")"
    rerun_ctl2() { local n_rerun_files=1 n_rerun_missing=0 n_rerun_outside=1; rerun_hashed; }
    check "control: rerun_hashed refuses a named file that is not there (change UP)" "$(ynnot rerun_ctl)"
    check "control: rerun_hashed refuses a named file outside <superseded> (change UP)" "$(ynnot rerun_ctl2)"
    check "control: under_superseded refuses <superseded> itself" "$(ynnot under_superseded "$SUPERSEDED_DIR")"
    check "control: under_superseded refuses a sibling directory sharing its prefix" "$(ynnot under_superseded "${SUPERSEDED_DIR}x/f")"
    check "control: under_superseded takes a file inside it" "$(yn under_superseded "$SUPERSEDED_DIR/f")"
    n_cargo=$(pgrep -x cargo | wc -l)
    n_rustc=$(pgrep -x rustc | wc -l)
    echo "SERIALIZED: no other log run was in flight; cargo processes at entry: $n_cargo; rustc processes at entry: $n_rustc; this log builds in <repo> into <target>/main, one cargo command at a time (change QB)"
    no_build_running() { [ "$((n_cargo + n_rustc))" = 0 ]; }
    check "no cargo or rustc process was running at entry" "$(yn no_build_running)"
    echo "root: <repo> stands for the repository's top level (inside <home>, so scrubbed first); scripts/counting.sh, the spec, the chartsheet test module, the previous phase's test.log, part 7 P3's test.log, M6 part 2 P3's API record, chart_write.rs at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit and crates/emend/src are read from it by git show or git archive at the phase commit, the working spec is hashed in it, cargo test, clippy and doc run in it with their output in <target>/main, and the API record is installed in its records unless TEST_RECORDS_DEST names another (changes UX, VJ, VK, VW, VZ, WS and WY)"
    echo "root: <home> stands for the home directory of the account that ran this script"
    echo "root: <phase> stands for <home>/.cache/emend-build/m6p3-p3, the phase's directory on the disk; <phase>/gen/defined.py, the defined-helper program, is copied from it (changes UF, UO, UX, VK, VR, WF, WL and WY)"
    echo "root: <scripts> stands for <phase>/scripts, this script's own directory on the disk, which holds the script, the formatter <scripts>/make_review.py beside it (generated by gen/test.py; change WU) and, in <scripts>/out, its own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    echo "root: <api> stands for <phase>/api unless TEST_API_DIR names another (a dry run's stand-in), the directory T1 writes the listing into, <api>/listing.tsv and <api>/files.tsv, refused if either is there (change WS)"
    echo "root: <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3 stands for part 7 P3's phase directory, whose gen/api-listing.py (the listing program) T1 copies; <home>/.cache/emend-build/m6p2-p3 for M6 part 2 P3's, whose api/listing.tsv is the listing this one is compared with; both read only (changes VW and WT)"
    echo "root: <target> stands for <phase>/target, the phase's one target root (specs/0001); <target>/main holds this log's builds (cargo test on both targets, clippy, doc)"
    echo "root: <build> stands for the build root on the disk, <phase>/test unless TEST_BUILD names another"
    echo "root: <superseded> stands for <phase>/superseded, where a rerun's superseded files are kept; read only"
    echo "root: <scratch>/w stands for this run's mktemp -d working directory under <build>, kept on the disk after the run (change QC): <scratch>/w/counting.sh the phase commit's library, sourced; the captured cargo outputs (*.out); <scratch>/w/prev-test.log, the previous phase's test.log read at the phase commit; <scratch>/w/chartsheet.rs, the chartsheet test module read at the phase commit, and <scratch>/w/chartsheet-tests, its tests as read; <scratch>/w/defined.py, the defined-helper program copied, and its outputs; <scratch>/w/api, T1's work: the archive of crates/emend/src, the listing program copied, its fixture crate, the keys and gate sets, chart_write.rs at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit and the staged record; the controls' fixtures (changes RD, UF, UK, UL, UQ, UX, VJ, VK, VW, WE, WF, WS and WY)"
    
    apart() { case "$1/" in "$2"/*) return 1 ;; esac; case "$2/" in "$1"/*) return 1 ;; esac; return 0; }
    roots_distinct() { apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$MAIN" && apart "$BUILD_ROOT" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$MAIN" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$SUPERSEDED_DIR" "$SELF_DIR" && apart "$SUPERSEDED_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" && apart "$SUPERSEDED_DIR" "$MAIN" && apart "$TARGET_DIR" "$BUILD_ROOT" && apart "$TARGET_DIR" "$MAIN"; }
    check "the roots other than <home> and <phase> are distinct, none inside another (<scratch>/w inside <build>)" "$(yn roots_distinct)"
    roots_ctl() { apart "$B" "$BUILD_ROOT"; }
    check "control: apart refuses <scratch>/w against <build>, which holds it" "$(ynnot roots_ctl)"
    echo "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set in this shell: $([ -n "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    key_unset() { [ -z "${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY:-}" ]; }
    check "ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is not set" "$(yn key_unset)"
    key_set_ctl() { local ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=planted; key_unset; }
    check "control: the same check refuses a shell where the variable is set" "$(ynnot key_set_ctl)"
    echo "at entry: status lines $entry_all; of them this phase's logs or its API record $entry_own; planning's working spec, admitted at PLANNING_SPEC: $entry_plan; the two read by the accounted pattern: $entry_ours; the lines (change WW):"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the phase commit given to this script: $C"
    echo "  git rev-parse HEAD at this run:        $(git rev-parse HEAD)"
    echo "  the controls' commits: the null commit $NULL_SHA; the fabricated commit $FAKE_SHA (the given one, its last hex digit changed); the short sha $SHORT_SHA"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is a full sha" "$(yn full_sha "$C")"
    check "the phase commit given to this script is HEAD" "$(yn head_is "$C")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$NULL_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a fabricated commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$FAKE_SHA")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a short sha of the real commit" "$(ynnot given_ok "$SHORT_SHA")"
    short_names_head() { [ "$(git rev-parse "$SHORT_SHA")" = "$(git rev-parse HEAD)" ]; }
    check "control: the short sha is the real commit's, so only its form is refused" "$(yn short_names_head)"
    ours_ctl() { printf ' M scripts/check.sh\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified gate file" "$(ynnot ours_ctl)"
    ours_src_ctl() { printf ' M crates/emend/src/cells.rs\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified crate source" "$(ynnot ours_src_ctl)"
    ours_roadmap_ctl() { printf ' M ROADMAP.md\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified ROADMAP.md (committed and clean in this phase; changes UY, VG, VT, WB and WP)" "$(ynnot ours_roadmap_ctl)"
    if plan_admitted; then n_ours_ctl_want=3; else n_ours_ctl_want=2; fi
    ours_rec_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m6p3-p3/gate.log\n?? records/api-review-m6p3-2026-01-01-%s.md\n?? records/logs/m6p3-p2/gate.log\n?? records/logs/m6p3-p3x/gate.log\n M records/logs/m6p3-p3/gate.log\n M ROADMAP.md\n M specs/0040-analytic-chart-elements.md\n?? records/m6p3-p3-chartaxis-2026-01-01-%s.md\n?? records/api-review-m6p3-2026-01-01-%s.md.x\n?? records/api-review-m6p3-2026-01-01-%s.txt\n?? records/api-review-m6p2-2026-01-01-%s.md\n?? records/size-m6p3-2026-01-01-%s.md\n?? records/api-review-m6p3-2026-01-01-0000000.md\n' "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" "$SHORT_SHA" | count_matches -E "$OURS" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern takes this phase's untracked log and its API record alone, no other phase's log, no sibling directory, no tracked log, no modified roadmap, the modified spec only when planning's copy is admitted, no run record, no longer name, no .txt, no other part's API record, no size record and no other commit's (changes RA, UA, UI, UR, UY, VG, VJ, VM, WB, WE, WH, WP and WS)" "$(yn [ "$(ours_rec_ctl)" = "$n_ours_ctl_want" ])"
    # Change WW (ruling S): the own pattern takes the phase's two paths and not
    # the working spec; the plan line takes the working spec alone.
    own_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m6p3-p3/gate.log\n?? records/api-review-m6p3-2026-01-01-%s.md\n M specs/0040-analytic-chart-elements.md\n?? records/logs/m6p3-p2/gate.log\n' "$SHORT_SHA" | count_matches -E "$OWN" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the own pattern takes the phase's log and its API record and not the working spec (change WW)" "$(yn [ "$(own_ctl)" = 2 ])"
    plan_line_ctl() { printf '?? records/logs/m6p3-p3/gate.log\n M specs/0040-analytic-chart-elements.md\n M specs/0039-chart-kinds-and-formatting.md\n' | count_matches -E "$PLAN_LINE" /dev/stdin; }
    check "control: the plan line pattern takes the working spec's line alone (change WW)" "$(yn [ "$(plan_line_ctl)" = 1 ])"
    ours_readme_ctl() { printf ' M README.md\n' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE "$OURS"; }
    check "control: the phase's status pattern refuses a modified README.md (committed and clean in this phase; changes UA, UI, UR, UY and VG)" "$(ynnot ours_readme_ctl)"
    SPEC_HAVE=$(sha256sum <"$SPEC" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    SPEC_BLOB=$(git show "$C:$SPEC" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$SPEC | sha256sum: $SPEC_BLOB; sha256sum $SPEC (the working file; changes RA, UA, UI, UR and UY): $SPEC_HAVE"
    check "the spec's blob at the phase commit is at the hash this log pins" "$(yn [ "$SPEC_BLOB" = "$SPEC_WANT" ])"
    spec_working() { [ "$SPEC_HAVE" = "$SPEC_WANT" ] || { plan_admitted && [ "$SPEC_HAVE" = "$PLANNING_SPEC" ]; }; }
    check "the working spec is that blob, or planning's working copy at PLANNING_SPEC when given (changes UY, VG and VM)" "$(yn spec_working)"
    spec_working_ctl() { local PLANNING_SPEC= SPEC_HAVE=$FAKE_SHA; spec_working; }
    check "control: spec_working refuses another hash with no PLANNING_SPEC (change VM)" "$(ynnot spec_working_ctl)"
    plan_ctl() { local PLANNING_SPEC=$FAKE_SHA; plan_admitted; }
    check "control: plan_admitted refuses a PLANNING_SPEC the working file does not hash to (change VM)" "$(ynnot plan_ctl)"
    spec_ctl() { [ "$(printf 'x' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)" = "$SPEC_WANT" ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the hash of another file" "$(ynnot spec_ctl)"
    echo
    echo "## script that wrote this log"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$SELF"
    echo
    echo "## the shared counting library this log sources"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/counting.sh"
    echo
    echo "## counting controls"
    counting_controls
    if [ "$counting_controls_ok" != yes ]; then fail=1; fi
    
    # failed_names <cargo output>: prints the name of every test the run failed,
    # from its FAILED lines, or "none" (M5 part 6's form). It prints, so it is
    # never a check's condition.
    failed_names() {
      local n
      n=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '^test .* \.\.\. FAILED$' "$1" | sed -E 's/^test (.*) \.\.\. FAILED$/\1/')
      if [ -n "$n" ]; then printf '%s\n' "$n" | sed 's/^/    failed test: /'; else echo "    failed tests: none"; fi
    }
    printf 'test a::b ... ok\ntest a::c ... FAILED\n' >"$B/c-failed"
    check "control: failed_names prints the name of the one FAILED line of two" "$(yn [ "$(failed_names "$B/c-failed")" = "    failed test: a::c" ])"
    printf 'test a::b ... ok\n' >"$B/c-failed-none"
    check "control: failed_names prints none for a run with no FAILED line" "$(yn [ "$(failed_names "$B/c-failed-none")" = "    failed tests: none" ])"
    # diag_lines <cargo output>: the lines a warning or an error begins with
    # (rustc's and clippy's "warning:" / "warning[...]" / "error:" / "error[...]"),
    # counted by the counting library's form.
    DIAG='^(warning|error)(\[[A-Za-z0-9_:]+\])?: '
    diag_lines() { count_matches -E "$DIAG" "$1"; }
    printf 'warning: unused import\nerror[E0433]: failed to resolve\n    Finished x\nnote: this is not one\n' >"$B/c-diag"
    check "control: diag_lines counts the two diagnostic lines of a four-line fixture" "$(yn [ "$(diag_lines "$B/c-diag")" = 2 ])"
    
    CT=$TARGET_DIR/main
    SETS="off charts charts,images charts,comments charts,read all"
    # set_args <set>: the cargo arguments of a feature set.
    set_args() { case $1 in off) ;; all) echo "--all-features" ;; *) echo "--features $1" ;; esac; }
    # test_run <name> <cargo args...>: runs cargo with the args into <target>/main,
    # keeps the output as <name>.out, prints the exit, the summary lines and the
    # failed names, and writes <name>.rc, .passed, .failed and .nok. It prints,
    # so it is never a check's condition; run_passed reads its files.
    test_run() {
      local name=$1 rc passed failed nok
      shift
      echo "command: CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo $*"
      CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CT cargo "$@" >"$B/$name.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
      rc=$?
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E '^test result: ' "$B/$name.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
      failed_names "$B/$name.out"
      passed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/$name.out")
      failed=$(awk '/^test result: / { for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;$/) n += $i } END { print n + 0 }' "$B/$name.out")
      nok=$(count_matches -E '^test .* \.\.\. ok$' "$B/$name.out")
      echo "$rc" >"$B/$name.rc"; echo "$passed" >"$B/$name.passed"; echo "$failed" >"$B/$name.failed"; echo "$nok" >"$B/$name.nok"
      echo "  $name: exit $rc; passed $passed; failed $failed; executed (passed plus failed) $((passed + failed)); test lines ending ok $nok"
    }
    # run_passed <name>: exit 0, failed 0, passed more than 0 and equal to the ok lines.
    run_passed() {
      local rc passed failed nok
      rc=$(cat "$B/$1.rc"); passed=$(cat "$B/$1.passed"); failed=$(cat "$B/$1.failed"); nok=$(cat "$B/$1.nok")
      [ "$rc" = 0 ] && [ "$failed" = 0 ] && [ "$passed" -gt 0 ] && [ "$passed" = "$nok" ]
    }
    echo 0 >"$B/c-run.rc"; echo 3 >"$B/c-run.passed"; echo 1 >"$B/c-run.failed"; echo 3 >"$B/c-run.nok"
    check "control: run_passed refuses a run with one failed test" "$(ynnot run_passed c-run)"
    echo 0 >"$B/c-run2.rc"; echo 3 >"$B/c-run2.passed"; echo 0 >"$B/c-run2.failed"; echo 2 >"$B/c-run2.nok"
    check "control: run_passed refuses a run whose passed count is not its ok lines" "$(ynnot run_passed c-run2)"
    echo 0 >"$B/c-run3.rc"; echo 3 >"$B/c-run3.passed"; echo 0 >"$B/c-run3.failed"; echo 3 >"$B/c-run3.nok"
    check "control: run_passed takes a clean run of three" "$(yn run_passed c-run3)"
    
    echo
    echo "## W: cargo test --workspace on both targets (the gate's own test steps)"
    test_run ws-host test --workspace
    check "W host: exit 0, none failed, some ran, passed equals the ok lines" "$(yn run_passed ws-host)"
    test_run ws-i686 test --workspace --target i686-unknown-linux-musl
    check "W i686: exit 0, none failed, some ran, passed equals the ok lines" "$(yn run_passed ws-i686)"
    
    echo
    echo "## F: cargo test -p emend with each of the spec's six feature sets, on both targets (change UJ)"
    for target in host i686; do
      for set in $SETS; do
        args=(test -p emend)
        [ "$target" = host ] || args+=(--target i686-unknown-linux-musl)
        # shellcheck disable=SC2207
        args+=($(set_args "$set"))
        test_run "f-$target-$set" "${args[@]}"
        check "F $target, features $set: exit 0, none failed, some ran, passed equals the ok lines" "$(yn run_passed "f-$target-$set")"
      done
    done
    more_with_all() { [ "$(cat "$B/f-$1-all.passed")" -gt "$(cat "$B/f-$1-off.passed")" ]; }
    check "F host: the all-features run passes more tests than the run with none (the sets differ)" "$(yn more_with_all host)"
    check "F i686: the all-features run passes more tests than the run with none" "$(yn more_with_all i686)"
    more_ctl() { [ "$(cat "$B/f-host-off.passed")" -gt "$(cat "$B/f-host-all.passed")" ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the reverse order" "$(ynnot more_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## E: each W and F run's passed count beside the previous phase's committed test.log, no run fewer, host equal to i686 (change UK)"
    PREV_TEST=records/logs/m6p3-p2/test.log
    PREV_FORM='^  (ws|f)-(host|i686)[^:]*: exit 0; passed [0-9]+; failed 0; '
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$PREV_TEST > <scratch>/w/prev-test.log; grep -cE '$PREV_FORM' <scratch>/w/prev-test.log"
    git show "$C:$PREV_TEST" >"$B/prev-test.log"
    rc_prev=$?
    n_prev=$(count_matches -E "$PREV_FORM" "$B/prev-test.log")
    echo "  exit $rc_prev; run lines $n_prev"
    prev_read() { [ "$rc_prev" = 0 ] && [ "$n_prev" = 14 ]; }
    check "the previous phase's test.log was read at the phase commit, its run lines 14 (two workspace runs and six sets on each target)" "$(yn prev_read)"
    # prev_count <log> <run name>: the passed figure of the log's one line
    # "  <run name>: exit 0; passed <n>; failed 0; ...", the test log's form for
    # a run this log repeats under the same name; "none" when not exactly one
    # line reads so. It prints, so its value is compared.
    prev_count() {
      local hits
      hits=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -E "^  $2: exit 0; passed [0-9]+; failed 0; " "$1" | sed -E 's/^  [^:]*: exit 0; passed ([0-9]+); .*$/\1/')
      if [ -n "$hits" ] && [ "$(printf '%s\n' "$hits" | wc -l)" = 1 ]; then echo "$hits"; else echo none; fi
    }
    # same_count <a> <b>: both are the same decimal number.
    same_count() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9]+$' && [ "$1" = "$2" ]; }
    # not_fewer <a> <b>: both decimal numbers, a not below b.
    not_fewer() { printf '%s' "$1" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9]+$' && printf '%s' "$2" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -qE '^[0-9]+$' && [ "$1" -ge "$2" ]; }
    printf '%s\n' '  f-host-off: exit 0; passed 10; failed 0; executed (passed plus failed) 10; test lines ending ok 10' \
      '  f-host-offx: exit 0; passed 11; failed 0; executed (passed plus failed) 11; test lines ending ok 11' \
      '  f-host-all: exit 0; passed 12; failed 0; executed (passed plus failed) 12; test lines ending ok 12' \
      '  f-host-all: exit 0; passed 13; failed 0; executed (passed plus failed) 13; test lines ending ok 13' \
      '  f-host-charts: exit 101; passed 14; failed 1; executed (passed plus failed) 15; test lines ending ok 14' >"$B/c-prevtest"
    check "control: prev_count reads 10 for f-host-off, not the figure of the longer name f-host-offx" "$(yn [ "$(prev_count "$B/c-prevtest" f-host-off)" = 10 ])"
    check "control: prev_count reads none for a run the log gives twice (f-host-all)" "$(yn [ "$(prev_count "$B/c-prevtest" f-host-all)" = none ])"
    check "control: prev_count reads none for a run that did not exit 0 with none failed (f-host-charts)" "$(yn [ "$(prev_count "$B/c-prevtest" f-host-charts)" = none ])"
    check "control: prev_count reads none for a run the log does not give (f-host-images)" "$(yn [ "$(prev_count "$B/c-prevtest" f-host-images)" = none ])"
    check "control: same_count refuses 515 against 516" "$(ynnot same_count 515 516)"
    check "control: same_count refuses none against none" "$(ynnot same_count none none)"
    check "control: same_count takes 515 against 515" "$(yn same_count 515 515)"
    check "control: not_fewer refuses 514 against 515" "$(ynnot not_fewer 514 515)"
    check "control: not_fewer refuses none against 515" "$(ynnot not_fewer none 515)"
    check "control: not_fewer takes 515 against 515" "$(yn not_fewer 515 515)"
    # e_line <run name>: prints the run's figure, its previous one and the
    # difference, and checks it is not fewer; a run the previous log did not
    # give is printed as new.
    e_line() {
      local want have
      want=$(prev_count "$B/prev-test.log" "$1")
      have=$(cat "$B/$1.passed")
      if [ "$want" = none ]; then
        echo "  E $1: the previous test.log gives no run of this name; this run passed $have"
        echo none >"$B/$1.prev"
      else
        echo "  E $1: the previous test.log $want; this run passed $have; difference $((have - want))"
        echo "$want" >"$B/$1.prev"
      fi
    }
    for name in ws-host ws-i686; do
      e_line "$name"
      check "E $name: a previous figure exists and this run's is not fewer (change UK)" "$(yn not_fewer "$(cat "$B/$name.passed")" "$(cat "$B/$name.prev")")"
    done
    for target in host i686; do
      for set in $SETS; do
        e_line "f-$target-$set"
        check "E $target, features $set: a previous figure exists and this run's is not fewer (changes UK and US)" "$(yn not_fewer "$(cat "$B/f-$target-$set.passed")" "$(cat "$B/f-$target-$set.prev")")"
      done
    done
    # Change US: each run's figure is the one this phase expects.
    # expected <run name>: the figure the generator typed in for the run.
    expected() {
      case $1 in
        ws-*) echo 1386 ;;
        f-*-off) echo 515 ;;
        f-*-charts) echo 666 ;;
        f-*-charts,images) echo 708 ;;
        f-*-charts,comments) echo 711 ;;
        f-*-charts,read) echo 769 ;;
        f-*-all) echo 1148 ;;
        *) echo none ;;
      esac
    }
    for name in ws-host ws-i686 $(for target in host i686; do for set in $SETS; do echo "f-$target-$set"; done; done); do
      echo "  E $name: this run passed $(cat "$B/$name.passed"); the figure this phase expects $(expected "$name")"
      check "E $name: the figure this phase expects, P2's (changes US, VH, VO, VU, WC, WI and WQ)" "$(yn same_count "$(cat "$B/$name.passed")" "$(expected "$name")")"
    done
    check "control: expected gives none for a run this log does not make (f-host-images)" "$(yn [ "$(expected f-host-images)" = none ])"
    check "control: same_count refuses the expected charts figure less one against it (change US)" "$(ynnot same_count "$(( $(expected f-host-charts) - 1 ))" "$(expected f-host-charts)")"
    check "E: the workspace's host figure equals its i686 figure" "$(yn same_count "$(cat "$B/ws-host.passed")" "$(cat "$B/ws-i686.passed")")"
    for set in $SETS; do
      check "E features $set: the host figure equals the i686 figure" "$(yn same_count "$(cat "$B/f-host-$set.passed")" "$(cat "$B/f-i686-$set.passed")")"
    done
    plus_one=$(( $(cat "$B/f-host-off.passed") + 1 ))
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the host off run's count plus one" "$(ynnot same_count "$plus_one" "$(cat "$B/f-i686-off.passed")")"
    minus_one=$(( $(cat "$B/f-host-off.prev") - 1 ))
    check "control: not_fewer refuses the previous host off figure less one against it" "$(ynnot not_fewer "$minus_one" "$(cat "$B/f-host-off.prev")")"
    
    echo
    echo "## N: the chartsheet module's tests and the part's P2 tests ran and passed by name (changes UL, UT, VA, VI, VP, VV, WD, WJ and WR)"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:crates/emend/src/package/tests/chartsheet.rs > <scratch>/w/chartsheet.rs; awk <each #[test] fn's name, with the feature of a #[cfg(feature = ...)] line before it> > <scratch>/w/chartsheet-tests"
    git show "$C:crates/emend/src/package/tests/chartsheet.rs" >"$B/chartsheet.rs"
    rc_rs=$?
    # read_tests <file>: one line per #[test] fn, its name then the feature a
    # cfg line just before the #[test] gates it on, or none.
    read_tests() {
      awk '/^#\[cfg\(feature = "[a-z]+"\)\]$/ { f = $0; sub(/^#\[cfg\(feature = "/, "", f); sub(/"\)\]$/, "", f); next }
        /^#\[test\]$/ { t = 1; next }
        t && /^fn [a-z0-9_]+\(\) \{$/ { n = $2; sub(/\(.*$/, "", n); print n, (f == "" ? "none" : f); t = 0; f = ""; next }
        !/^#\[/ { f = "" }' "$1"
    }
    read_tests "$B/chartsheet.rs" >"$B/chartsheet-tests"
    n_tests=$(count_lines "$B/chartsheet-tests")
    n_img=$(count_matches -E ' images$' "$B/chartsheet-tests")
    n_cmt=$(count_matches -E ' comments$' "$B/chartsheet-tests")
    n_none=$(count_matches -E ' none$' "$B/chartsheet-tests")
    echo "  exit $rc_rs; tests $n_tests; gated on images $n_img; on comments $n_cmt; on neither $n_none:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$B/chartsheet-tests"
    tests_read() { [ "$rc_rs" = 0 ] && [ "$n_tests:$n_img:$n_cmt:$n_none" = "20:1:1:18" ]; }
    check "the module's tests read at run time are the generator's reading: 20, 1 gated on images, 1 on comments, 18 on neither, none new (changes UT, VI, VP and WD)" "$(yn tests_read)"
    printf '%s\n' '#[cfg(feature = "images")]' '#[test]' 'fn a() {' '}' '#[test]' 'fn b() {' '}' '#[cfg(feature = "comments")]' 'fn helper() {' '}' '#[test]' 'fn c() {' '}' 'fn d() {' >"$B/c-tests.rs"
    check "control: read_tests reads a images, b none and c none from a fixture whose cfg on a helper does not carry to the next test" "$(yn [ "$(read_tests "$B/c-tests.rs" | tr '\n' ';')" = "a images;b none;c none;" ])"
    # wants <set> <feature>: whether a run of the set enables the test's features
    # (every set but off enables charts).
    wants() {
      case "$1:$2" in
        off:*) return 1 ;;
        *:none) return 0 ;;
        all:*) return 0 ;;
        charts,images:images | charts,comments:comments) return 0 ;;
      esac
      return 1
    }
    check "control: wants refuses an images test in the charts,comments set" "$(ynnot wants charts,comments images)"
    check "control: wants refuses an ungated test in the off set" "$(ynnot wants off none)"
    check "control: wants takes a comments test in the all set" "$(yn wants all comments)"
    # ok_lines <output> <full test name>: the run's lines "test <name> ... ok".
    ok_lines() { count_matches -xF "test $2 ... ok" "$1"; }
    MOD=package::tests::chartsheet
    # names_ok <run> <set>: every module test the set wants has one ok line, every
    # other none, and the run's ok lines of the module are exactly the wanted
    # ones.
    names_ok() {
      local name feat want=0 have
      while read -r name feat; do
        if wants "$2" "$feat"; then
          want=$((want + 1))
          [ "$(ok_lines "$B/$1.out" "$MOD::$name")" = 1 ] || return 1
        else
          [ "$(ok_lines "$B/$1.out" "$MOD::$name")" = 0 ] || return 1
        fi
      done <"$B/chartsheet-tests"
      have=$(count_matches -E "^test $MOD::[a-z0-9_]+ [.][.][.] ok$" "$B/$1.out")
      [ "$have" = "$want" ]
    }
    printf '%s\n' "test $MOD::$(head -n 1 "$B/chartsheet-tests" | cut -d' ' -f1) ... FAILED" >"$B/c-names.out"
    check "control: ok_lines reads 0 for a module test whose line is FAILED" "$(yn [ "$(ok_lines "$B/c-names.out" "$MOD::$(head -n 1 "$B/chartsheet-tests" | cut -d' ' -f1)")" = 0 ])"
    check "control: names_ok refuses that output for the charts set" "$(ynnot names_ok c-names charts)"
    for target in host i686; do
      for set in $SETS; do
        nm=$(count_matches -E "^test $MOD::[a-z0-9_]+ [.][.][.] ok$" "$B/f-$target-$set.out")
        echo "  N $target, features $set: the module's ok lines $nm"
        check "N $target, features $set: each module test the set enables passed by name, no other ran (change UL)" "$(yn names_ok "f-$target-$set" "$set")"
      done
    done
    for target in host i686; do
      nm=$(count_matches -E "^test $MOD::[a-z0-9_]+ [.][.][.] ok$" "$B/ws-$target.out")
      echo "  N ws-$target: the module's ok lines $nm"
      check "N ws-$target: every module test passed by name (the workspace's features unified as all of the tool's: charts, images, comments)" "$(yn names_ok "ws-$target" all)"
    done
    # Changes WD, WJ and WR: the part's P2 tests by name, typed by P2's
    # generator from P2's phase commit's sources (each once there, ungated in
    # its module); P3 adds no test and changes no test file (checked by
    # gen/test.py).
    NEW_LIB="package::tests::chart_write::the_plot_lines_are_taken_by_the_kinds_that_take_them_and_refused_by_the_others package::tests::chart_write::the_plot_lines_are_written_after_the_series_and_before_the_marker_and_the_axis_ids package::tests::chart_write::the_axis_options_are_taken_by_each_kind_s_axes_by_their_form_and_refused_by_the_round_kinds package::tests::chart_write::the_scaling_is_written_in_the_schema_s_order_and_the_units_and_skips_in_their_places package::tests::chart_write::a_date_axis_takes_the_category_axis_s_place_with_its_units package::tests::chart_write::the_axis_field_rules_are_refused package::tests::chart_write::the_plot_lines_and_the_axes_follow_the_check_order"
    NEW_TOOL="the_chart_axis_sample_adds_a_line_a_scatter_and_a_column_and_reads_them_back the_chart_axis_sample_writes_each_plot_line_and_axis_form the_chart_axis_sample_references_at_most_a_thousand_rows"
    echo "  the part's P2 crate tests: $(printf '%s\n' $NEW_LIB | count_lines /dev/stdin); the tool's: $(printf '%s\n' $NEW_TOOL | count_lines /dev/stdin)"
    # new_lines <run> <names>: the sum of the names' ok lines in the run. It
    # prints, so its value is compared.
    new_lines() {
      local t n=0
      for t in $2; do n=$((n + $(ok_lines "$B/$1.out" "$t"))); done
      echo "$n"
    }
    # each_once <run> <names>: every name has exactly one ok line in the run.
    each_once() {
      local t
      for t in $2; do [ "$(ok_lines "$B/$1.out" "$t")" = 1 ] || return 1; done
    }
    for target in host i686; do
      for set in $SETS; do
        nl=$(new_lines "f-$target-$set" "$NEW_LIB")
        echo "  N $target, features $set: the part's P2 crate tests' ok lines $nl"
        if [ "$set" = off ]; then
          check "N $target, features $set: none of the part's P2 tests ran (the set has no charts; changes VI, VP, WD and WR)" "$(yn [ "$nl" = 0 ])"
        else
          check "N $target, features $set: each of the part's 7 P2 crate tests passed once by name (changes VI, VP, WD, WJ and WR)" "$(yn each_once "f-$target-$set" "$NEW_LIB")"
        fi
      done
    done
    for target in host i686; do
      echo "  N ws-$target: the part's P2 crate tests' ok lines $(new_lines "ws-$target" "$NEW_LIB"); the tool's $(new_lines "ws-$target" "$NEW_TOOL")"
      check "N ws-$target: each of the part's P2 crate tests and the tool's 3 passed once by name (changes VI, VP, WD, WJ and WR)" "$(yn each_once "ws-$target" "$NEW_LIB $NEW_TOOL")"
    done
    printf 'test %s ... ok\n' $NEW_LIB >"$B/c-new.out"
    sed '1s/ ok$/ FAILED/' "$B/c-new.out" >"$B/c-new2.out"
    check "control: each_once takes a fixture holding each P2 crate test's ok line once (changes VI, WD and WR)" "$(yn each_once c-new "$NEW_LIB")"
    check "control: each_once refuses the same fixture with the first line FAILED" "$(ynnot each_once c-new2 "$NEW_LIB")"
    check "control: each_once refuses the fixture for the tool's tests, which it does not hold" "$(ynnot each_once c-new "$NEW_TOOL")"
    n_new_ctl=$(new_lines c-new "$NEW_LIB")
    n_new_ctl2=$(new_lines c-new2 "$NEW_LIB")
    check "control: new_lines reads one fewer in the FAILED fixture" "$(yn [ "$n_new_ctl2" = "$((n_new_ctl - 1))" ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## R: each F run's doc-tests result, 0 passed and 0 failed (change RC, kept; change UM)"
    # doc_result <cargo output>: "<passed> <failed>" of the first "test result:"
    # line after cargo's "Doc-tests emend" line, or "none". It prints, so its
    # value is compared.
    doc_result() {
      local r
      r=$(awk '/^[[:space:]]*Doc-tests emend[[:space:]]*$/ { d = 1; next }
        d && /^test result: / { p = 0; f = 0; for (i = 1; i < NF; i++) { if ($(i + 1) ~ /^passed;$/) p = $i; if ($(i + 1) ~ /^failed;$/) f = $i }; print p, f; exit }' "$1")
      if [ -n "$r" ]; then echo "$r"; else echo none; fi
    }
    printf 'test result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored\n   Doc-tests emend\n\nrunning 1 test\ntest result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored\n' >"$B/c-doc1"
    check "control: doc_result reads 1 0 for a fixture with one doctest, not the lib line before it" "$(yn [ "$(doc_result "$B/c-doc1")" = "1 0" ])"
    printf 'test result: ok. 5 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored\n' >"$B/c-doc2"
    check "control: doc_result reads none for an output with no Doc-tests line" "$(yn [ "$(doc_result "$B/c-doc2")" = none ])"
    for target in host i686; do
      for set in $SETS; do
        dl=$(count_matches -E '^[[:space:]]*Doc-tests emend[[:space:]]*$' "$B/f-$target-$set.out")
        dr=$(doc_result "$B/f-$target-$set.out")
        echo "  R $target, features $set: Doc-tests emend lines $dl; its result (passed failed) $dr"
        check "R $target, features $set: one Doc-tests emend line, its result 0 passed 0 failed" "$(yn [ "$dl:$dr" = "1:0 0" ])"
      done
    done
    
    clean_run() { [ "$(cat "$B/$1.rc")" = 0 ] && [ "$(diag_lines "$B/$1.out")" = 0 ]; }
    # lint_run <name> <env...> -- <cargo args...>: runs cargo into <target>/main,
    # prints the exit and the diagnostic line count, writes <name>.rc.
    lint_run() {
      local name=$1 rc
      shift
      echo "command: CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main $*"
      env CARGO_TARGET_DIR="$CT" "$@" >"$B/$name.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
      rc=$?
      echo "$rc" >"$B/$name.rc"
      echo "  $name: exit $rc; diagnostic lines $(diag_lines "$B/$name.out")"
      LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -E "$DIAG" "$B/$name.out" | sed 's/^/    /'
    }
    echo 0 >"$B/c-lint.rc"; printf 'warning: unused variable\n    Finished x\n' >"$B/c-lint.out"
    check "control: clean_run refuses an exit-0 run with one warning line" "$(ynnot clean_run c-lint)"
    echo 0 >"$B/c-lint2.rc"; printf '    Checking x\n    Finished x\n' >"$B/c-lint2.out"
    check "control: clean_run takes an exit-0 run with none" "$(yn clean_run c-lint2)"
    
    echo
    echo "## C: clippy with -D warnings, the crate's six sets, the workspace and the size probe crate's three (changes UE, UJ and UN)"
    for set in $SETS; do
      # shellcheck disable=SC2207
      sa=($(set_args "$set"))
      lint_run "c-$set" cargo clippy -p emend --all-targets "${sa[@]}" -- -D warnings
      check "C features $set: exit 0, 0 diagnostic lines" "$(yn clean_run "c-$set")"
    done
    lint_run c-workspace cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
    check "C workspace: exit 0, 0 diagnostic lines" "$(yn clean_run c-workspace)"
    PROBE_SETS="emend,xml charts images"
    for set in $PROBE_SETS; do
      lint_run "c-probe-$set" cargo clippy -p size-probe --all-targets --features "$set" -- -D warnings
      check "C size-probe, features $set: exit 0, 0 diagnostic lines (change UE)" "$(yn clean_run "c-probe-$set")"
    done
    
    echo
    echo "## D: rustdoc with -D warnings, the crate's six sets (change UJ)"
    for set in $SETS; do
      # shellcheck disable=SC2207
      sa=($(set_args "$set"))
      lint_run "d-$set" RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' cargo doc -p emend --no-deps "${sa[@]}"
      check "D features $set: exit 0, 0 diagnostic lines" "$(yn clean_run "d-$set")"
    done
    
    TAB=$(printf '\t')
    PROG_SRC=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/gen/api-listing.py
    OLD_LISTING=$HOME/.cache/emend-build/m6p2-p3/api/listing.tsv
    OLD_RECORD=records/api-review-m6p2-2026-10-20-50a3989.md
    FORMATTER=$SELF_DIR/make_review.py
    T=$B/api
    mkdir -p "$T" || fail=1
    
    echo
    echo "## T1: the pub listing, every pub item of crates/emend reachable from the crate root, by module (specs/0040 \"P3\"; M6 part 2 P3's form; changes WS and WT)"
    api_absent() { [ ! -e "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" ] && [ ! -e "$API_DIR/files.tsv" ]; }
    check "no listing is in <api> before this run" "$(yn api_absent)"
    mkdir -p "$API_DIR" "$T/src" "$T/py" "$T/fx/src" || fail=1
    echo "### the listing program, part 7 P3's own"
    cp "$PROG_SRC" "$T/py/api-listing.py" || fail=1
    PROG_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$T/py/api-listing.py" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    P7_PROG_SHA=$(git show "$C:records/logs/m3p7-p3/test.log" | awk '/^command: the listing program, written by this script/ { getline; print $1; exit }')
    echo "command: cp <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p7-p3/gen/api-listing.py <scratch>/w/api/py/api-listing.py; sha256sum: $PROG_SHA"
    echo "command: the line after part 7's \"command: the listing program\" line in records/logs/m3p7-p3/test.log at the phase commit (git show): ${P7_PROG_SHA:-none}"
    prog_is_p7() { [ -n "$P7_PROG_SHA" ] && [ "$PROG_SHA" = "$P7_PROG_SHA" ]; }
    check "the listing program is the one part 7 P3's test log inserted and ran, by hash" "$(yn prog_is_p7)"
    prog_ctl() { local PROG_SHA; PROG_SHA=$(printf 'x' | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1); prog_is_p7; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the hash of another file" "$(ynnot prog_ctl)"
    echo "command: git archive <phase commit> crates/emend/src | tar -x -C <scratch>/w/api/src"
    git archive "$C" crates/emend/src | tar -x -C "$T/src"
    arch_rc=$?
    n_arch=$(find "$T/src/crates/emend/src" -type f -name '*.rs' | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    n_tree=$(git ls-tree -r --name-only "$C" crates/emend/src | count_matches -E '[.]rs$' /dev/stdin)
    echo "  archive exit: $arch_rc; .rs files extracted: $n_arch; .rs files under crates/emend/src in the phase commit's tree: $n_tree"
    arch_ok() { [ "$arch_rc" = 0 ] && [ "$n_arch" -ge 1 ] && [ "$n_arch" = "$n_tree" ]; }
    check "the archive holds every .rs file of the phase commit's crates/emend/src" "$(yn arch_ok)"
    arch_ctl() { local n_tree=$((n_tree + 1)); arch_ok; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses a tree count one more than the archive's" "$(ynnot arch_ctl)"
    
    echo "### the program's control: part 7's fixture crate, written by this log"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub mod a;' 'mod b;' '#[cfg(test)]' 'mod tests;' 'pub use b::{X, Y as Z};' '/// pub fn not_this()' 'pub(crate) fn hidden() {}' >"$T/fx/src/lib.rs"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub struct P {' '    pub f: u8,' '    g: u8,' '}' 'impl P { pub fn m(&self) { let _s = "{ pub fn fake"; } }' '#[cfg(feature = "q")]' 'pub const C: u8 = 1;' >"$T/fx/src/a.rs"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub struct X;' 'pub struct W;' 'pub enum Y {' '    V,' '}' 'impl W {' '    pub fn n() {}' '}' >"$T/fx/src/b.rs"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub fn t() {}' >"$T/fx/src/tests.rs"
    for f in lib.rs a.rs b.rs tests.rs; do
      echo "  <scratch>/w/api/fx/src/$f:"
      sed 's/^/      /' "$T/fx/src/$f"
    done
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/api/py/api-listing.py <scratch>/w/api/fx/src fx <repo> <phase commit> <scratch>/w/api/fx/rows.tsv <scratch>/w/api/fx/files.tsv --no-added"
    python3 -I -B "$T/py/api-listing.py" "$T/fx/src" fx "$MAIN" "$C" "$T/fx/rows.tsv" "$T/fx/files.tsv" --no-added >"$T/fx/out" 2>"$T/fx/err"
    fx_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $fx_rc; standard output $(wc -c <"$T/fx/out") bytes; standard error $(wc -c <"$T/fx/err") bytes; its rows, columns 2 to 8, tabs shown as |:"
    cut -f2-8 "$T/fx/rows.tsv" | tr '\t' '|' | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  its files table, tabs shown as |:"
    tr '\t' '|' <"$T/fx/files.tsv" | sed 's/^/    /'
    exp_line() { local IFS=$TAB; printf '%s\n' "$*"; }
    {
      exp_line file line kind name container cfg reachable
      exp_line fx/lib.rs 1 mod a - - yes
      exp_line fx/lib.rs 5 use 'b::{X, Y as Z}' - - yes
      exp_line fx/a.rs 1 struct P - - yes
      exp_line fx/a.rs 2 field f P - yes
      exp_line fx/a.rs 5 method m P - yes
      exp_line fx/a.rs 7 const C - q yes
      exp_line fx/b.rs 1 struct X - - 'yes (re-exported as crate::X)'
      exp_line fx/b.rs 2 struct W - - 'no (private module, not re-exported)'
      exp_line fx/b.rs 3 enum Y - - 'yes (re-exported as crate::Z)'
      exp_line fx/b.rs 7 method n W - 'no (its type is not reachable)'
    } >"$T/fx/expected-rows"
    {
      exp_line file module rows rows_at_line_start rows_reachable
      exp_line fx/lib.rs crate 2 2 2
      exp_line fx/a.rs crate::a 4 3 4
      exp_line fx/b.rs crate::b 4 4 2
      exp_line fx/tests 'cfg(test), not walked' - - -
    } >"$T/fx/expected-files"
    cut -f2-8 "$T/fx/rows.tsv" >"$T/fx/got-rows"
    fx_ran() { [ "$fx_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$T/fx/out" ] && [ ! -s "$T/fx/err" ]; }
    check "control: the program exits 0 on the fixture crate and prints nothing" "$(yn fx_ran)"
    check "control: the fixture's rows are the expected ones (part 7's fixture and expectation)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/fx/got-rows" "$T/fx/expected-rows")"
    check "control: the fixture's files table is the expected one" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/fx/files.tsv" "$T/fx/expected-files")"
    cp "$T/fx/expected-rows" "$T/fx/c-rows"; printf 'x\n' >>"$T/fx/c-rows"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the expected rows with one line more" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/fx/got-rows" "$T/fx/c-rows")"
    PUB_RE='^[[:space:]]*pub '
    n_fx_a=$(count_matches -E "$PUB_RE" "$T/fx/src/a.rs")
    n_fx_lib=$(count_matches -E "$PUB_RE" "$T/fx/src/lib.rs")
    echo "  command: count_matches -E '$PUB_RE' over the fixture's a.rs and lib.rs: $n_fx_a and $n_fx_lib"
    check "control: the grep form counts a.rs's three line-start pub lines" "$(yn [ "$n_fx_a" = 3 ])"
    check "control: the grep form counts lib.rs's two pub lines" "$(yn [ "$n_fx_lib" = 2 ])"
    
    echo "### the listing of the phase commit's crate"
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scratch>/w/api/py/api-listing.py <scratch>/w/api/src/crates/emend/src crates/emend/src <repo> <phase commit> <api>/listing.tsv <api>/files.tsv"
    python3 -I -B "$T/py/api-listing.py" "$T/src/crates/emend/src" crates/emend/src "$MAIN" "$C" "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" "$API_DIR/files.tsv" >"$T/listing.out" 2>"$T/listing.err"
    lst_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $lst_rc; standard output $(wc -c <"$T/listing.out") bytes; standard error $(wc -c <"$T/listing.err") bytes"
    listing_ran() { [ "$lst_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$T/listing.out" ] && [ ! -s "$T/listing.err" ]; }
    check "the listing program exits 0 and prints nothing" "$(yn listing_ran)"
    LISTING_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    FILES_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$API_DIR/files.tsv" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "  command: sha256sum <api>/listing.tsv <api>/files.tsv"
    echo "    $LISTING_SHA  listing.tsv"
    echo "    $FILES_SHA  files.tsv"
    echo "  the files table, tabs shown as |:"
    tr '\t' '|' <"$API_DIR/files.tsv" | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  the listing, tabs shown as |:"
    tr '\t' '|' <"$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | sed 's/^/    /'
    
    echo "### each walked file's pub lines by grep beside the listing's rows"
    echo "command: count_matches -E '$PUB_RE' <scratch>/w/api/src/<file>, for every walked file"
    pub_bad=0 nfiles=0 rows_sum=0
    while IFS=$TAB read -r f mod rows atstart reach; do
      [ "$f" = file ] && continue
      case "$rows" in -) continue ;; esac
      nfiles=$((nfiles + 1))
      rows_sum=$((rows_sum + rows))
      ng=$(count_matches -E "$PUB_RE" "$T/src/$f")
      echo "    $f ($mod): grep $ng; rows $rows; rows at line start $atstart; reachable $reach"
      if [ "$ng" != "$atstart" ]; then pub_bad=$((pub_bad + 1)); fi
      if [ "$rows" != "$atstart" ]; then
        echo "      rows whose pub follows other text on its line, which the grep form does not count: $((rows - atstart))"
      fi
    done <"$API_DIR/files.tsv"
    n_rows=$(($(count_lines "$API_DIR/listing.tsv") - 1))
    echo "  walked files: $nfiles; rows by the files table: $rows_sum; rows in the listing: $n_rows; files whose grep count differs from their rows at line start: $pub_bad"
    pub_agree() { [ "$nfiles" -ge 1 ] && [ "$pub_bad" = 0 ]; }
    check "every walked file's pub lines by grep equal the listing's rows at line start" "$(yn pub_agree)"
    rows_agree() { [ "$n_rows" -ge 1 ] && [ "$n_rows" = "$rows_sum" ]; }
    check "the listing's rows are the files table's rows, summed" "$(yn rows_agree)"
    pub_ctl() { local pub_bad=1; pub_agree; }
    check "control: the same check refuses one file differing" "$(ynnot pub_ctl)"
    find "$T/src/crates/emend/src" -type f -name '*.rs' | sed "s#^$T/src/##" | sort >"$T/all-rs"
    awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 && $3 != "-" { print $1 }' "$API_DIR/files.tsv" | sort >"$T/walked"
    awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 && $2 ~ /^cfg\(test\)/ { print $1 }' "$API_DIR/files.tsv" | sort >"$T/skipped"
    # unaccounted <file list>: the .rs files neither walked nor under a skipped
    # cfg(test) module (its file, or a path under its directory).
    unaccounted() {
      awk -v W="$T/walked" -v S="$T/skipped" 'BEGIN { while ((getline l < W) > 0) w[l] = 1; ns = 0; while ((getline l < S) > 0) s[++ns] = l }
        { if ($0 in w) next; ok = 0; for (i = 1; i <= ns; i++) if ($0 == s[i] ".rs" || index($0, s[i] "/") == 1) ok = 1; if (!ok) print }' "$1"
    }
    unaccounted "$T/all-rs" >"$T/unaccounted"
    n_all=$(count_lines "$T/all-rs")
    n_walked=$(count_lines "$T/walked")
    n_skipped=$(count_lines "$T/skipped")
    n_un=$(count_lines "$T/unaccounted")
    echo "  .rs files in the archive: $n_all; walked: $n_walked; cfg(test) modules not walked: $n_skipped; files neither walked nor under one: $n_un"
    sed 's/^/    unaccounted: /' "$T/unaccounted"
    check "every .rs file is walked or lies under a cfg(test) module" "$(yn [ "$n_un" = 0 ])"
    cp "$T/all-rs" "$T/c-all-rs"; printf 'crates/emend/src/extra.rs\n' >>"$T/c-all-rs"
    check "control: the same form finds one planted file neither walked nor under a test module" "$(yn [ "$(unaccounted "$T/c-all-rs" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    echo "  rows by kind:"
    awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 { print $4 }' "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    echo "  rows by reachable:"
    awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 { r = $8; sub(/ \(.*/, "", r); print r }' "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 { print $10 }' "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | sort -u >"$T/added"
    n_added=$(count_lines "$T/added")
    n_dash=$(awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 && $10 == "-"' "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    not_anc=0
    while read -r h; do
      [ "$h" = - ] && continue
      git merge-base --is-ancestor "$h" "$C" 2>/dev/null || not_anc=$((not_anc + 1))
    done <"$T/added"
    echo "  distinct added commits: $n_added; rows with no added commit (-): $n_dash; added commits not ancestors of the phase commit: $not_anc"
    check "every added commit is an ancestor of the phase commit" "$(yn [ "$not_anc" = 0 ])"
    anc_ctl() { git merge-base --is-ancestor 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 "$C" 2>/dev/null; }
    check "control: the same test refuses the null commit" "$(ynnot anc_ctl)"
    
    echo "### the rows, and the rows that differ from M6 part 2 P3's listing by key (change WT)"
    OLD_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$OLD_LISTING" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    REC_OLD_SHA=$(git show "$C:$OLD_RECORD" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E 'listing[.]tsv` sha256 [0-9a-f]{64}' | awk '{ print $3 }')
    n_old=$(($(count_lines "$OLD_LISTING") - 1))
    REC_OLD_ITEMS=$(git show "$C:$OLD_RECORD" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E '^- Items: [0-9]+,' | LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E '[0-9]+')
    echo "command: sha256sum <home>/.cache/emend-build/m6p2-p3/api/listing.tsv: $OLD_SHA; its rows (lines less the header): $n_old"
    echo "command: git show <phase commit>:$OLD_RECORD | grep -o -E 'listing[.]tsv\` sha256 <64 hex>': ${REC_OLD_SHA:-none}; its \"- Items: <n>,\" line's figure: ${REC_OLD_ITEMS:-none}"
    old_is_m4() { [ -n "$REC_OLD_SHA" ] && [ "$OLD_SHA" = "$REC_OLD_SHA" ]; }
    check "M6 part 2 P3's listing file is the one its record names, by hash" "$(yn old_is_m4)"
    old_ctl() { local OLD_SHA=$LISTING_SHA; old_is_m4; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses this phase's listing" "$(ynnot old_ctl)"
    old_rows_ok() { [ "$n_old" = 776 ] && [ "${REC_OLD_ITEMS:-none}" = 776 ]; }
    check "M6 part 2 P3's listing holds 776 rows, the figure its record states (change WT)" "$(yn old_rows_ok)"
    old_rows_ctl() { local n_old=777; old_rows_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses 777" "$(ynnot old_rows_ctl)"
    # keys_of <listing.tsv>: one line per row, its key (module, kind, name,
    # container, cfg, added; columns 1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10) joined by |, sorted.
    keys_of() { awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 { print $1 "|" $4 "|" $5 "|" $6 "|" $7 "|" $10 }' "$1" | LC_ALL=C sort; }
    keys_of "$OLD_LISTING" >"$T/keys-old"
    keys_of "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" >"$T/keys-new"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$T/keys-old" "$T/keys-new" >"$T/gone.got"
    LC_ALL=C comm -13 "$T/keys-old" "$T/keys-new" >"$T/new.got"
    n_gone=$(count_lines "$T/gone.got")
    n_new=$(count_lines "$T/new.got")
    echo "command: keys (module|kind|name|container|cfg|added) of M6 part 2 P3's listing and of this one, sorted, compared with comm"
    echo "  M6 part 2 P3's rows: $(count_lines "$T/keys-old"); this listing's rows: $(count_lines "$T/keys-new"); M6 part 2 P3's not here: $n_gone; this listing's not in M6 part 2 P3's: $n_new; equal by key: $(LC_ALL=C comm -12 "$T/keys-old" "$T/keys-new" | count_lines /dev/stdin)"
    echo "  M6 part 2 P3's rows not here:"
    sed 's/^/    - /' "$T/gone.got"
    echo "  this listing's rows not in M6 part 2 P3's:"
    sed 's/^/    + /' "$T/new.got"
    # The two sets the generator's static run of the same program over the
    # phase commit gave, checked by gen/test.py (change WT): one gone, the
    # charts re-export of crate::package, whose name list the part's nine new
    # types grow, so its key changes; forty new, that re-export's new key and
    # the part's thirty-nine new rows.
    printf '%s\n' 'crate::package|use|chart_write::{ DashStyle, LabelPosition, MarkerSymbol, NewChart, NewCombined, NewLabels, NewLine, NewMarker, NewPlot, NewPoint, NewSeries, NewSeriesName, OfPieKind, OfPieSplit, RadarStyle, }|-|charts|4c36f05' >"$T/gone.exp"
    printf '%s\n' 'crate::package::chart_write|enum|ErrorBarKind|-|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|enum|ErrorDirection|-|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|enum|ErrorValue|-|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|enum|TimeUnit|-|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|enum|TrendlineKind|-|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|backward|NewTrendline|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|base_unit|NewDateAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|category_axis|NewChart|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|date|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|direction|NewErrorBars|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|drop_lines|NewChart|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|end_cap|NewErrorBars|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|error_bars|NewSeries|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|forward|NewTrendline|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|high_low_lines|NewChart|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|intercept|NewTrendline|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|kind|NewErrorBars|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|kind|NewTrendline|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|log_base|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|major_unit|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|major|NewDateAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|max|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|minor_unit|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|minor|NewDateAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|min|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|name|NewTrendline|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|reversed|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|show_equation|NewTrendline|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|show_r_squared|NewTrendline|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|tick_label_skip|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|tick_mark_skip|NewAxis|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|trendline|NewSeries|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|up_down_bars|NewChart|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|value_axis|NewChart|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|value|NewErrorBars|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|struct|NewAxis|-|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|struct|NewDateAxis|-|charts|3c1f1f3' 'crate::package::chart_write|struct|NewErrorBars|-|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package::chart_write|struct|NewTrendline|-|charts|12f1314' 'crate::package|use|chart_write::{ DashStyle, ErrorBarKind, ErrorDirection, ErrorValue, LabelPosition, MarkerSymbol, NewAxis, NewChart, NewCombined, NewDateAxis, NewErrorBars, NewLabels, NewLine, NewMarker, NewPlot, NewPoint, NewSeries, NewSeriesName, NewTrendline, OfPieKind, OfPieSplit, RadarStyle, TimeUnit, TrendlineKind, }|-|charts|4c36f05' >"$T/new.exp"
    n_gone_exp=$(count_lines "$T/gone.exp"); n_new_exp=$(count_lines "$T/new.exp")
    echo "  the expected sets as typed: $n_gone_exp gone, $n_new_exp new"
    check "the typed sets hold one gone key, the re-export's, and forty new keys (change WT)" "$(yn [ "$n_gone_exp:$n_new_exp" = 1:40 ])"
    check "the row of M6 part 2 P3's listing gone from this one is the charts re-export's alone (change WT)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/gone.got" "$T/gone.exp")"
    check "the rows of this listing new against M6 part 2 P3's are the forty typed (change WT)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/new.got" "$T/new.exp")"
    { cat "$T/gone.exp"; printf '%s\n' 'crate::cells|struct|Planted|-|-|0000000'; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-gone.exp"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the gone set with one key planted" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/gone.got" "$T/c-gone.exp")"
    { cat "$T/new.exp"; printf '%s\n' 'crate::cells|struct|Planted|-|-|0000000'; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-new.exp"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the new set with one key planted" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/new.got" "$T/c-new.exp")"
    echo "  rows in the listing: $n_rows; M6 part 2 P3's $n_old, less $n_gone gone, plus $n_new new: $((n_old - n_gone + n_new))"
    rows_sum_ok() { [ "$n_rows" = "$((n_old - n_gone + n_new))" ] && [ "$n_rows" = 815 ]; }
    check "the listing holds 815 rows, M6 part 2 P3's 776 with one gone and forty new (change WT)" "$(yn rows_sum_ok)"
    rows_sum_ctl() { local n_rows=816; rows_sum_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses 816" "$(ynnot rows_sum_ctl)"
    echo "### the new rows' added commits, each by its subject: the part's two core commits, and an earlier commit the listing's heuristic dates five declaration lines to; no row widened (change WT)"
    by_subj() { git log --format='%H' -n 1 -F --grep="$1" "$C"; }
    added_bad=0
    for pair in "12f1314|M6 part 3 P1: charts write, trendlines and error bars" "3c1f1f3|M6 part 3 P2: charts write, plot lines and axis options" "4c36f05|M5 part 4 P1: charts write, add_chart for bar and line charts"; do
      short=${pair%%|*}; subj=${pair#*|}
      full=$(git rev-parse --verify -q "$short^{commit}"); want=$(by_subj "$subj")
      echo "  $short: $full; the commit of \"$subj\": ${want:-none}"
      if [ -z "$full" ] || [ "$full" != "$want" ]; then added_bad=$((added_bad + 1)); fi
    done
    check "each of the three is the commit of its subject (change WT)" "$(yn [ "$added_bad" = 0 ])"
    awk -F'|' '$6 != "12f1314" && $6 != "3c1f1f3"' "$T/new.got" >"$T/new-other.got"
    echo "  new rows whose added commit is neither of the part's core commits: $(count_lines "$T/new-other.got")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/new-other.got"
    # The heuristic's five, typed (change WT): NewChart's category_axis and
    # value_axis fields, NewTrendline's name and NewErrorBars' value, each a
    # line equal to one an earlier commit's type already held in the same file,
    # and the re-export's new key, whose first line is the old re-export's.
    printf '%s\n' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|category_axis|NewChart|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|name|NewTrendline|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|value_axis|NewChart|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package::chart_write|field|value|NewErrorBars|charts|4c36f05' 'crate::package|use|chart_write::{ DashStyle, ErrorBarKind, ErrorDirection, ErrorValue, LabelPosition, MarkerSymbol, NewAxis, NewChart, NewCombined, NewDateAxis, NewErrorBars, NewLabels, NewLine, NewMarker, NewPlot, NewPoint, NewSeries, NewSeriesName, NewTrendline, OfPieKind, OfPieSplit, RadarStyle, TimeUnit, TrendlineKind, }|-|charts|4c36f05' >"$T/new-other.exp"
    check "they are the five the listing's heuristic dates to M5 part 4 P1's commit (change WT)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/new-other.got" "$T/new-other.exp")"
    { cat "$T/new-other.exp"; printf '%s\n' 'crate::package|const|PLANTED|-|-|0000000'; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-new-other.exp"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the typed five with one row planted (change WT)" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/new-other.got" "$T/c-new-other.exp")"
    # A widened row: a new row equal to a gone row by module, kind, name,
    # container and added commit, its cfg alone differing (change WT).
    cut -d'|' -f1-4,6 "$T/new.got" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/new-bare"
    cut -d'|' -f1-4,6 "$T/gone.got" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/gone-bare"
    LC_ALL=C comm -12 "$T/new-bare" "$T/gone-bare" >"$T/widened.got"
    echo "  new rows equal to a gone row but for the cfg: $(count_lines "$T/widened.got")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/widened.got"
    check "no new row is a gone row with its cfg widened (change WT)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$T/widened.got")" = 0 ])"
    { cat "$T/new-bare"; printf '%s\n' 'crate::package|enum|Planted|-|0000000'; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-new-bare"
    { cat "$T/gone-bare"; printf '%s\n' 'crate::package|enum|Planted|-|0000000'; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-gone-bare"
    check "control: the same form finds one widened row with a key planted in both the new and the gone rows" "$(yn [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -12 "$T/c-new-bare" "$T/c-gone-bare" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    added_ctl() { [ "$(git rev-parse --verify -q "d8479f5^{commit}")" = "$(by_subj "M6 part 3 P2: charts write, plot lines and axis options")" ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses P2's doc commit against P2's core commit's subject" "$(ynnot added_ctl)"
    echo "### the items the feature gates widened to charts, pub or not, since M6 part 2 P3's listing (specs/0040 \"P3\"; change WT)"
    # Every cfg(any(...)) line naming charts that the diff over package.rs adds,
    # from M6 part 2 P3's phase commit (its listing's commit) to this one, and the
    # item it gates: the first line after it that is neither an attribute nor a
    # removed line, read for const, fn, enum or struct and its name. Change ZH:
    # an item read so whose declaration package.rs at M6 part 2 P3's phase
    # commit does not hold is a new item under the shared gate, not a
    # widening; the two sets are split and each compared with its typed list
    # (change WT: no widening and no new item under the shared gate), and both
    # go to the formatter (change WT).
    M2P3=$(by_subj "M6 part 2 P3: the CHANGELOG names the chart kinds and formatting")
    # gate_widenings: name|cfg line, one per item, from a diff on stdin. It
    # prints, so it writes files, never conditions.
    gate_widenings() {
      awk '
        /^\+[[:space:]]*#\[cfg\(any\(.*feature = "charts"/ { w = 1; c = substr($0, 2); sub(/^[[:space:]]+/, "", c); next }
        w && /^[ +]/ {
          l = substr($0, 2)
          if (l ~ /^[[:space:]]*#\[/) next
          if (match(l, /(const|fn|enum|struct) [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*/)) { n = substr(l, RSTART, RLENGTH); sub(/^[a-z]+ /, "", n); print n "|" c }
          w = 0
        }' | LC_ALL=C sort
    }
    echo "command: git diff <M6 part 2 P3's phase commit> <phase commit> -- crates/emend/src/package.rs | gate_widenings (M6 part 2 P3's phase commit by its subject: ${M2P3:-none})"
    git diff "$M2P3" "$C" -- crates/emend/src/package.rs | gate_widenings >"$T/gates-all.got"
    echo "  items the added any(...) lines naming charts gate: $(count_lines "$T/gates-all.got"):"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/gates-all.got"
    # declared_before <name>: package.rs at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit holds a
    # const, fn, enum or struct of that name (change WT).
    git show "$M2P3:crates/emend/src/package.rs" >"$T/package-before.rs"
    declared_before() { [ "$(count_matches -E "(const|fn|enum|struct) $1([^A-Za-z0-9_]|\$)" "$T/package-before.rs")" -ge 1 ]; }
    : >"$T/gates.got"; : >"$T/gates-new.got"
    while IFS='|' read -r gname gcfg; do
      if declared_before "$gname"; then printf '%s|%s\n' "$gname" "$gcfg" >>"$T/gates.got"; else printf '%s|%s\n' "$gname" "$gcfg" >>"$T/gates-new.got"; fi
    done <"$T/gates-all.got"
    echo "  of them declared in package.rs at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit, widened: $(count_lines "$T/gates.got"):"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/gates.got"
    echo "  not declared there, new items under the shared gate: $(count_lines "$T/gates-new.got"):"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/gates-new.got"
    check "control: declared_before finds DrawingRoot at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit" "$(yn declared_before DrawingRoot)"
    check "control: declared_before refuses NewAxis, which this part adds, in chart_write.rs" "$(ynnot declared_before NewAxis)"
    # The widened and the new the generator's run of the same form gave,
    # checked by gen/test.py (change WT): none of either.
    : >"$T/gates.exp"
    : >"$T/gates-new.exp"
    check "the typed widenings and new items are none (change WT)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$T/gates.exp"):$(count_lines "$T/gates-new.exp")" = 0:0 ])"
    check "no item the gates widened since M6 part 2 P3's phase commit (change WT)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/gates.got" "$T/gates.exp")"
    check "no new item under the shared gate since it (change WT)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/gates-new.got" "$T/gates-new.exp")"
    { cat "$T/gates.exp"; printf '%s\n' 'PLANTED|#[cfg(any(feature = "images", feature = "charts"))]'; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-gates.exp"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the typed widenings with one item planted" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/gates.got" "$T/c-gates.exp")"
    printf '%s\n' ' /// x' '-#[cfg(feature = "images")]' '+#[cfg(any(feature = "images", feature = "charts"))]' ' #[derive(Debug)]' ' pub enum Planted {' '+#[cfg(feature = "charts")]' '+mod planted;' '+    #[cfg(any(feature = "comments", feature = "charts"))]' '     fn planted_fn() {}' >"$T/c-gates.diff"
    gate_widenings <"$T/c-gates.diff" >"$T/c-gates.got"
    check "control: the same form reads two items from a fixture diff, past a derive line and an indent, not the new module's plain gate" "$(yn [ "$(cut -d'|' -f1 "$T/c-gates.got" | tr '\n' ' ')" = 'Planted planted_fn ' ])"
    cut -d'|' -f3 "$T/widened.got" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/widened-names"
    cut -d'|' -f1 "$T/gates.got" | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/gates-names"
    echo "  of them pub, in the listing (the widened rows' names): $(count_lines "$T/widened-names"); crate-private, not in the pub listing: $(LC_ALL=C comm -13 "$T/widened-names" "$T/gates-names" | count_lines /dev/stdin)"
    pub_among() { [ "$(count_lines "$T/widened-names")" = 0 ] && [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$T/widened-names" "$T/gates-names" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 0 ]; }
    check "no widened row is in the pub listing (change WT)" "$(yn pub_among)"
    printf 'Planted\n' >"$T/c-widened-names"
    check "control: the same form finds a planted widened name outside the gates list" "$(yn [ "$(LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$T/c-widened-names" "$T/gates-names" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ])"
    
    echo "### the chart writer's messages, none new; the row that lost Eq; NewPlot's variants (specs/0040 \"Errors\", \"P3\": \"the rows that lose Eq marked\"; change WV)"
    CW=crates/emend/src/package/chart_write.rs
    echo "command: git show <M6 part 2 P3's phase commit>:$CW > <scratch>/w/api/chart_write-before.rs (the commit by its subject: ${M2P3:-none})"
    git show "$M2P3:$CW" >"$T/chart_write-before.rs"
    before_rc=$?
    echo "  exit $before_rc; $(count_lines "$T/chart_write-before.rs") lines"
    # msgs_of <file>: the crate-private Error constants the file declares, one
    # name per line, sorted. It prints, so its value is compared.
    msgs_of() { awk 'index($0, "pub(crate) const ") == 1 && $4 == "Error" { n = $3; sub(/:$/, "", n); print n }' "$1" | LC_ALL=C sort; }
    msgs_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs" >"$T/msgs-before"
    msgs_of "$T/src/$CW" >"$T/msgs-now"
    echo "command: msgs_of over <scratch>/w/api/chart_write-before.rs and <scratch>/w/api/src/$CW"
    echo "  at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit: $(count_lines "$T/msgs-before"); now: $(count_lines "$T/msgs-now"); now: $(paste -sd' ' "$T/msgs-now")"
    msgs_same() { [ "$before_rc" = 0 ] && [ -s "$T/msgs-before" ] && cmp -s "$T/msgs-before" "$T/msgs-now"; }
    check "the chart writer's crate-private messages are the same set as at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit, the part adding none (change WV)" "$(yn msgs_same)"
    { cat "$T/msgs-now"; printf '%s\n' CHART_PLANTED; } | LC_ALL=C sort >"$T/c-msgs"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the set with one name planted" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/msgs-before" "$T/c-msgs")"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub(crate) const PLANTED_A: Error =' 'pub(crate) const PLANTED_B: u8 = 1;' '    pub(crate) const PLANTED_C: Error =' >"$T/c-msgs.rs"
    check "control: msgs_of reads a line-start Error constant and neither a u8 one nor an indented one" "$(yn [ "$(msgs_of "$T/c-msgs.rs" | paste -sd' ' -)" = PLANTED_A ])"
    check "control: msgs_of reads CHART_VALUE_RANGE, part 2's message, at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -xF CHART_VALUE_RANGE "$T/msgs-before")" = 1 ])"
    # derive_of <file> <kind> <name>: the derive line just before the pub item
    # of that kind and name, or none. It prints, so its value is compared.
    derive_of() { awk -v d="pub $2 $3" 'index($0, d " ") == 1 || index($0, d "<") == 1 || $0 == d " {" { print (p ~ /^#\[derive\(/ ? p : "none"); f = 1; exit } { p = $0 } END { if (!f) print "none" }' "$1"; }
    # key_rows <listing> <kind> <name>: the module-level rows of that kind and
    # name in crate::package::chart_write, as keys.
    key_rows() { awk -F"$TAB" -v k="$2" -v n="$3" 'NR > 1 && $1 == "crate::package::chart_write" && $4 == k && $5 == n && $6 == "-" { print $1 "|" $4 "|" $5 "|" $6 "|" $7 "|" $10 }' "$1"; }
    # eq_dropped <kind> <name>: Eq before and not now, its one row equal by key
    # in both listings.
    eq_dropped() {
      [ "$(derive_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs" "$1" "$2")" = '#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]' ] || return 1
      [ "$(derive_of "$T/src/$CW" "$1" "$2")" = '#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]' ] || return 1
      [ "$(key_rows "$OLD_LISTING" "$1" "$2" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 1 ] || return 1
      [ "$(key_rows "$OLD_LISTING" "$1" "$2")" = "$(key_rows "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" "$1" "$2")" ]
    }
    : >"$T/eq.got"
    for pair in 'struct|NewSeries'; do
      ek=${pair%%|*}; en=${pair#*|}
      echo "  $en ($ek): at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit $(derive_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs" "$ek" "$en"); now $(derive_of "$T/src/$CW" "$ek" "$en"); its row in M6 part 2 P3's listing $(key_rows "$OLD_LISTING" "$ek" "$en"); in this one $(key_rows "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" "$ek" "$en")"
      check "$en lost Eq, PartialEq kept, its one row equal by key in both listings, so the record marks it (specs/0040 \"P3\"; change WV)" "$(yn eq_dropped "$ek" "$en")"
      if eq_dropped "$ek" "$en"; then printf '%s|%s|%s|%s|%s\n' "$en" "$ek" "crate::package::chart_write" '#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]' '#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq)]' >>"$T/eq.got"; fi
    done
    echo "  NewChart (struct): at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit $(derive_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs" struct NewChart); now $(derive_of "$T/src/$CW" struct NewChart)"
    check "control: eq_dropped refuses NewChart, which derives PartialEq without Eq at both commits" "$(ynnot eq_dropped struct NewChart)"
    check "control: eq_dropped refuses NewSeries read as an enum" "$(ynnot eq_dropped enum NewSeries)"
    printf '%s\n' '#[derive(Debug)]' 'pub struct Planted {' '#[derive(Clone)]' 'pub enum PlantedE<' 'pub struct PlantedNot;' >"$T/c-derive.rs"
    check "control: derive_of reads a struct's derive and an enum's before a generic, and none past the end" "$(yn [ "$(derive_of "$T/c-derive.rs" struct Planted);$(derive_of "$T/c-derive.rs" enum PlantedE);$(derive_of "$T/c-derive.rs" struct Absent)" = '#[derive(Debug)];#[derive(Clone)];none' ])"
    # derives_of <file>: every pub struct and enum at line start with its
    # derive line, one kind|name|derive line each, sorted. It prints, so its
    # value is compared.
    derives_of() { awk 'match($0, /^pub (struct|enum) [A-Za-z0-9_]+/) { split(substr($0, RSTART, RLENGTH), w, " "); print w[2] "|" w[3] "|" (p ~ /^#\[derive\(/ ? p : "none") } { p = $0 }' "$1" | LC_ALL=C sort; }
    derives_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs" >"$T/derives-before"
    derives_of "$T/src/$CW" >"$T/derives-now"
    LC_ALL=C comm -23 "$T/derives-before" "$T/derives-now" >"$T/derives-changed"
    echo "command: derives_of over both chart_write.rs files; the lines at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit not now"
    echo "  pub structs and enums then: $(count_lines "$T/derives-before"); now: $(count_lines "$T/derives-now"); lines then not now: $(count_lines "$T/derives-changed")"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/derives-changed"
    printf '%s\n' 'struct|NewSeries|#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]' >"$T/derives-changed.exp"
    check "the one pub struct or enum whose derive changed is NewSeries's, Eq dropped; every other one both commits hold keeps its derive (change WV)" "$(yn cmp -s "$T/derives-changed" "$T/derives-changed.exp")"
    check "control: the same comparison refuses the expectation with NewChart's line planted" "$(ynnot cmp -s "$T/derives-changed" "$T/derives-before")"
    echo "  the rows marked, for the formatter: $(count_lines "$T/eq.got")"
    check "the one row that lost Eq goes to the formatter (change WV)" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$T/eq.got")" = 1 ])"
    # variants_of <file>: NewPlot's variant lines, from its declaration to its
    # closing brace, the lines at four spaces' indent that open a variant.
    variants_of() { awk '$0 == "pub enum NewPlot {" { f = 1; next } f && $0 == "}" { exit } f && /^    [A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*( \{|,)$/ { print }' "$1"; }
    echo "  NewPlot's variant lines: at M6 part 2 P3's phase commit $(variants_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs" | count_lines /dev/stdin); now $(variants_of "$T/src/$CW" | count_lines /dev/stdin)"
    variants_same() { [ "$(variants_of "$T/src/$CW" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 16 ] && [ "$(variants_of "$T/chart_write-before.rs")" = "$(variants_of "$T/src/$CW")" ]; }
    check "NewPlot's sixteen variant lines are M6 part 2 P3's, the part adding none (change WV)" "$(yn variants_same)"
    printf '%s\n' 'pub enum NewPlot {' '    Bar {' '    Stock,' '    /// x' '    Planted { y: u8 },' '}' '    After,' >"$T/c-variants.rs"
    check "control: variants_of reads a fixture's two variant lines and not a doc line, a one-line variant or a line past the brace" "$(yn [ "$(variants_of "$T/c-variants.rs" | count_lines /dev/stdin)" = 2 ])"
    
    echo
    echo "## T2: the doc build with every feature and no warning, and the documented items it indexes (M6 part 2 P3's form; change WS)"
    echo "command: RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' CARGO_TARGET_DIR=<target>/main cargo doc --offline -p emend --no-deps --all-features"
    RUSTDOCFLAGS='-D warnings' CARGO_TARGET_DIR=$CT cargo doc --offline -p emend --no-deps --all-features >"$T/doc.out" 2>&1 </dev/null
    doc_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $doc_rc; its output:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/doc.out"
    check "the doc build exits 0" "$(yn [ "$doc_rc" = 0 ])"
    WARN_RE='^(warning|error)'
    nwarn=$(count_matches -E "$WARN_RE" "$T/doc.out")
    check "no warning or error line in its output: $nwarn" "$(yn [ "$nwarn" = 0 ])"
    printf 'warning: x\n   Finished\nerror: y\n' >"$T/c-doc"
    check "control: the same form counts two such lines in a fixture" "$(yn [ "$(count_matches -E "$WARN_RE" "$T/c-doc")" = 2 ])"
    ALL_HTML=$CT/doc/emend/all.html
    ITEM_RE='<li><a href="[^"]+"'
    # item_links <html>: one line per item link of a rustdoc all-items page.
    item_links() { LC_ALL=C "$G" -o -E "$ITEM_RE" "$1"; }
    item_links "$ALL_HTML" >"$T/all-items" 2>/dev/null
    n_links=$(count_lines "$T/all-items")
    n_anchors=$(count_matches -E '^<li><a href="#' "$T/all-items")
    n_documented=$((n_links - n_anchors))
    echo "command: grep -o -E '$ITEM_RE' <target>/main/doc/emend/all.html | count_lines; of them, the links to a section anchor (href starting #)"
    echo "  link lines in the index: $n_links; section anchors among them: $n_anchors; documented module-level items: $n_documented; by kind (the link's last path segment up to its first dot):"
    sed -E 's#^<li><a href="([^"]*/)?([A-Za-z_]+)[.].*#\2#' "$T/all-items" | sort | uniq -c | sed 's/^/    /'
    check "the index lists at least one documented item" "$(yn [ "$n_documented" -ge 1 ])"
    printf '<h3>Structs</h3><ul class="all-items"><li><a href="#structs">S</a></li><li><a href="a/struct.A.html">a::A</a></li><li><a href="struct.B.html">B</a></li></ul><h3>Functions</h3><ul class="all-items"><li><a href="fn.f.html">f</a></li></ul>\n' >"$T/c-all.html"
    item_links "$T/c-all.html" >"$T/c-all-items"
    check "control: the same form finds four links, one of them an anchor, on one line of a fixture page" "$(yn [ "$(count_lines "$T/c-all-items"):$(count_matches -E '^<li><a href="#' "$T/c-all-items")" = 4:1 ])"
    n_top=$(awk -F"$TAB" 'NR > 1 && $8 ~ /^yes/ && ($4 == "struct" || $4 == "enum" || $4 == "fn" || $4 == "const" || $4 == "type" || $4 == "trait" || $4 == "static")' "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" | count_lines /dev/stdin)
    echo "  the listing's reachable module-level types, functions, constants, statics and aliases: $n_top"
    check "the documented module-level items equal the listing's reachable module-level items" "$(yn [ "$n_documented" = "$n_top" ])"
    top_ctl() { local n_top=$((n_top + 1)); [ "$n_documented" = "$n_top" ]; }
    check "control: the same comparison refuses one item more" "$(ynnot top_ctl)"
    
    echo
    echo "## R2: the API record, written by the formatter and installed (specs/0040 \"P3\"; changes WS and WU)"
    FMT_SHA=$(sha256sum <"$FORMATTER" | cut -d' ' -f1)
    echo "command: sed 's/^/    /' <scripts>/make_review.py; sha256sum: $FMT_SHA; $(wc -c <"$FORMATTER") bytes"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$FORMATTER"
    fmt_there() { [ -s "$FORMATTER" ]; }
    check "the formatter is there and not empty" "$(yn fmt_there)"
    check "control: the same check refuses a file that is not there" "$(ynnot [ -s "$SELF_DIR/no-such-formatter.py" ])"
    REC_DATE=$(date -u +%F)
    REC_NAME=api-review-m6p3-$REC_DATE-$SHORT_SHA.md
    STAGED=$T/$REC_NAME
    echo "command: python3 -I -B <scripts>/make_review.py <api>/listing.tsv <home>/.cache/emend-build/m6p2-p3/api/listing.tsv <scratch>/w/api/$REC_NAME $REC_DATE $SHORT_SHA <listing sha256> <files sha256> <formatter sha256> $n_links $n_anchors $n_documented $n_top <scratch>/w/api/gates.got <scratch>/w/api/gates-new.got <scratch>/w/api/eq.got"
    python3 -I -B "$FORMATTER" "$API_DIR/listing.tsv" "$OLD_LISTING" "$STAGED" "$REC_DATE" "$SHORT_SHA" "$LISTING_SHA" "$FILES_SHA" "$FMT_SHA" "$n_links" "$n_anchors" "$n_documented" "$n_top" "$T/gates.got" "$T/gates-new.got" "$T/eq.got" >"$T/fmt.out" 2>"$T/fmt.err"
    fmt_rc=$?
    echo "  exit: $fmt_rc; standard error $(wc -c <"$T/fmt.err") bytes; its standard output:"
    sed 's/^/    /' "$T/fmt.out"
    FMT_WANT="rows 815; {'keep': 815}; differing from M6 part 2 P3: 1 gone, 40 new; gate-widened 0, 0 of them pub; new under the shared gate 0; Eq dropped 1"
    fmt_ok() { [ "$fmt_rc" = 0 ] && [ ! -s "$T/fmt.err" ] && [ "$(cat "$T/fmt.out")" = "$FMT_WANT" ] && [ -s "$STAGED" ]; }
    check "the formatter exits 0, prints \"$FMT_WANT\" alone and writes its file" "$(yn fmt_ok)"
    fmt_ctl() { local FMT_WANT="rows 776; {'keep': 776}; differing from M6 part 2 P3: 1 gone, 20 new; gate-widened 0, 0 of them pub; new under the shared gate 0; Eq dropped 3"; fmt_ok; }
    check "control: the same check refuses M6 part 2 P3's line" "$(ynnot fmt_ctl)"
    n_nonascii=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd '\200-\377' <"$STAGED" | wc -c)
    echo "  the staged record: $(wc -c <"$STAGED") bytes, sha256 $(sha256sum <"$STAGED" | cut -d' ' -f1); non-ASCII bytes in it: $n_nonascii"
    check "the staged record is ASCII" "$(yn [ "$n_nonascii" = 0 ])"
    REC_DEST=$RECORDS_DEST/$REC_NAME
    rec_absent() { [ ! -e "$REC_DEST" ]; }
    echo "command: cp <scratch>/w/api/$REC_NAME <the records' destination>/$REC_NAME, refused if that name is there (the destination: $RECORDS_DEST)"
    if rec_absent; then
      cp "$STAGED" "$REC_DEST"
      inst_rc=$?
      echo "  installed: exit $inst_rc"
      check "the record's name was not there before this run" yes
    else
      inst_rc=refused
      echo "  refused: $REC_NAME is already there"
      check "the record's name was not there before this run" no
    fi
    installed_ok() { [ "$inst_rc" = 0 ] && cmp -s "$STAGED" "$REC_DEST"; }
    check "the installed record is the staged one, byte for byte" "$(yn installed_ok)"
    echo "  the installed record: $RECORDS_DEST/$REC_NAME, sha256 $(sha256sum <"$REC_DEST" 2>/dev/null | cut -d' ' -f1), $(wc -c <"$REC_DEST" 2>/dev/null) bytes"
    check "control: the absence check refuses the staged file, which is there" "$(ynnot [ ! -e "$STAGED" ])"
    
    
    echo
    echo "## the log itself"
    ALL=()
    for f in "$B"/*.out; do ALL+=("$f"); done
    nbytes=$(cat "${ALL[@]}" | LC_ALL=C tr -cd '\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177\200-\377' | wc -c)
    printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m y caf\303\251\n' >"$B/ctl-bytes"
    nctl=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd '\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177\200-\377' <"$B/ctl-bytes" | wc -c)
    echo "  captured outputs: ${#ALL[@]}; control and non-ASCII bytes in them: $nbytes; in a control file with two ESC and one two-byte character: $nctl"
    check "no control or non-ASCII byte in any captured output" "$(yn [ "$nbytes" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count finds four bytes in the control file" "$(yn [ "$nctl" = 4 ])"
    echo "command: git status --porcelain"
    git status --porcelain | sed 's/^/    /'
    st_all=$(run_lines git status --porcelain)
    st_ours=$(run_matches -E "$OURS" git status --porcelain)
    st_own=$(run_matches -E "$OWN" git status --porcelain)
    st_plan=$(run_matches -E "$PLAN_LINE" git status --porcelain)
    echo "status lines: $st_all; of them this phase's logs or its API record: $st_own; planning's working spec, admitted at PLANNING_SPEC: $st_plan; the two read by the accounted pattern: $st_ours (change WW)"
    status_accounted() { [ "$st_all" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" != error ] && [ "$st_all" = "$st_ours" ]; }
    check "every change in the working tree is this phase's logs, the API record this log installed or, when admitted, planning's working spec (changes UR, UY, VJ, WE, WS and WW)" "$(yn status_accounted)"
    own_sum() { [ "$st_own" != error ] && [ "$st_plan" != error ] && [ "$st_ours" = "$((st_own + st_plan))" ]; }
    check "the accounted lines are the own lines and the plan line, summed (change WW)" "$(yn own_sum)"
    echo
    echo "## this script's own standard error (specs/0017 P1 verification ruling 7)"
    nerr=$(wc -c <"$ERR")
    cp "$ERR" "$B/c-err"; printf 'x' >>"$B/c-err"
    nerr_ctl=$(wc -c <"$B/c-err")
    echo "  command: wc -c <scripts>/out/test.stderr: $nerr bytes; a copy with one byte appended: $nerr_ctl"
    check "this script wrote nothing to its standard error" "$(yn [ "$nerr" = 0 ])"
    check "control: the same count reads one byte more in the copy" "$(yn [ "$nerr_ctl" = "$((nerr + 1))" ])"
    echo "run ended at $(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)"
    echo "test log checks all as expected: $([ "$fail" -eq 0 ] && echo yes || echo no)"
    exec 1>&3
    wait "$SCRUB_PID" 2>/dev/null
    exit "$fail"

## the shared counting library this log sources
    # emend shared counting forms (specs/0007-gate-self-test.md, "scripts/counting.sh").
    #
    # Sourced by scripts/gate-self-test.sh and by the log scripts of later phases,
    # which use these instead of carrying their own copy.
    #
    # WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. In T3 P4 four counting sites compared a bare `grep -c`
    # with 0 without reading the exit status, so a read error printed 0 and the
    # check passed. Two independent checks found them, and the class was declared
    # closed three further times while instances still stood: a helper whose first
    # repair read grep's status while `cat` was the failing command, and both
    # halves of one function in T2 P7. Planning's remedy is that every counting
    # form, including a throwaway one, is a named function that reads the exit
    # status and has a positive control, from the start.
    #
    # Every function prints either a number or the word "error". None of them ever
    # prints a matched line, a value, or a path. A caller that compares a result
    # with 0 therefore cannot mistake a failed read for an absence.
    #
    # counting_controls runs every form against a match, a miss and an unreadable
    # file, prints one line per control, and sets counting_controls_ok. Callers run
    # it before using any form.
    
    G=/usr/bin/grep
    
    # count_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: total matching lines across the
    # files, or "error" if any file could not be read. The files go to grep
    # directly: with `cat file | grep -c`, an unreadable file makes CAT fail while
    # grep counts 0 over the empty stream and exits 1, so the read error reads as
    # "no hits".
    count_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_from_file <-F|-E> <pattern file> <file>...: the same, with the patterns
    # read from a file (grep -f), so a pattern is never printed.
    count_from_file() {
      local mode=$1 patterns=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c "$mode" -f "$patterns" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # count_bytes <tr class> <file>...: total bytes of that class across the files,
    # or "error" if any file could not be read. Each file is read on its own rather
    # than through `cat "$@" | tr`, for the same reason as above.
    count_bytes() {
      local class=$1 total=0 f n
      shift
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(LC_ALL=C tr -cd "$class" <"$f" | wc -c) || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_lines <file>...: total lines, or "error" if any file could not be read.
    count_lines() {
      local total=0 f n
      for f in "$@"; do
        [ -r "$f" ] || { printf 'error'; return; }
        n=$(wc -l <"$f") || { printf 'error'; return; }
        total=$((total + n))
      done
      printf '%s' "$total"
    }
    
    # count_matches_i <-F|-E> <pattern> <file>...: count_matches with -i, the form
    # the hygiene step uses for OFFICE_RE and ZONE_RE. It lived in a log script as a
    # hand-rolled copy with no control of its own (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap
    # 14); a counting form belongs here, with a control, even a throwaway one.
    count_matches_i() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$(LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -H -c -i "$mode" -e "$pattern" -- "$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ge 2 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | awk -F: '{ n += $NF } END { print n + 0 }'
    }
    
    # run_lines <command...>: run the command, and print the number of lines it
    # wrote on stdout, or "error" if the command itself failed. The log scripts
    # asserted a clean working tree with
    #   git status --porcelain >file 2>/dev/null || : >file
    # which turns a FAILED git status into an empty file, so the check read a
    # failed command as a clean tree (independent check 2, T6 P1, gap 1; planning
    # reproduced it). Reading the command's exit status is the whole point: a
    # command that could not run is never the same as a command that found nothing.
    run_lines() {
      local out rc
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | wc -l | tr -d ' '
    }
    
    # run_matches <-F|-E> <pattern> <command...>: the same, counting only the lines
    # that match, so a caller can compare "all lines" with "lines of the expected
    # shape" without either count hiding a failed command.
    run_matches() {
      local mode=$1 pattern=$2 out rc
      shift 2
      out=$("$@" 2>/dev/null); rc=$?
      if [ "$rc" -ne 0 ]; then printf 'error'; return; fi
      if [ -z "$out" ]; then printf '0'; return; fi
      printf '%s\n' "$out" | LC_ALL=C "$G" -a -c "$mode" -e "$pattern" || true
    }
    
    CTRL_CLASS='\000-\010\013\014\016-\037\177'
    NONASCII_CLASS='\200-\377'
    
    # counting_controls <label prefix>: run every counting form above against a
    # fixture that must match and one that must not, and against an unreadable
    # file, printing one line per result. Sets counting_controls_ok to yes or no.
    # This is the positive control planning requires for every form, and it also
    # proves each form reports "error" rather than 0 when it cannot read.
    counting_controls() {
      local d ok=yes r
      d=$(mktemp -d) || { counting_controls_ok=no; return; }
      printf 'alpha\nbeta needle gamma\nneedle\n' >"$d/hit"
      printf 'nothing of interest\n' >"$d/miss"
      printf 'x \033[31mred\033[m\017 y\ncaf\303\251\n' >"$d/bytes"
      printf 'needle\n' >"$d/patterns"
      printf 'unreadable\n' >"$d/locked"
      chmod 000 "$d/locked"
    
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit");        echo "  control count_matches on a file with two matching lines: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/miss");       echo "  control count_matches on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_matches summed over two files: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -E 'ne+dle' "$d/hit");      echo "  control count_matches with a regular expression: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/locked");     echo "  control count_matches on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/hit" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_matches on readable plus unreadable: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/hit"); echo "  control count_from_file on the same file: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/miss"); echo "  control count_from_file on a file with none: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_from_file -F "$d/patterns" "$d/locked"); echo "  control count_from_file on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/bytes");    echo "  control count_bytes, control bytes in a file with ESC, ESC and SI: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$NONASCII_CLASS" "$d/bytes"); echo "  control count_bytes, non-ASCII bytes in a file with one two-byte character: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/miss");     echo "  control count_bytes on a clean file: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_bytes "$CTRL_CLASS" "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_bytes on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/hit");                    echo "  control count_lines on a three-line file: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_lines "$d/locked");                 echo "  control count_lines on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      printf 'NEEDLE\nneedle\n' >"$d/mixedcase"
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/mixedcase"); echo "  control count_matches_i on mixed case: $r (expect 2)"; [ "$r" = 2 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches -F needle "$d/mixedcase");  echo "  control count_matches on the same file, case sensitive: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(count_matches_i -F needle "$d/locked");   echo "  control count_matches_i on an unreadable file: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines printf 'a\nb\nc\n');            echo "  control run_lines on a command printing three lines: $r (expect 3)"; [ "$r" = 3 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines true);                          echo "  control run_lines on a command printing nothing: $r (expect 0)"; [ "$r" = 0 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines false);                         echo "  control run_lines on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_lines "$d/no-such-command");          echo "  control run_lines on a command that cannot run: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle printf 'needle\nother\n'); echo "  control run_matches on a command printing one match: $r (expect 1)"; [ "$r" = 1 ] || ok=no
      r=$(run_matches -F needle false);             echo "  control run_matches on a FAILING command: $r (expect error)"; [ "$r" = error ] || ok=no
    
      chmod 644 "$d/locked"
      rm -rf "${d:?}"
      counting_controls_ok=$ok
      echo "  counting controls: $([ "$ok" = yes ] && echo "all as expected" || echo FAILED)"
    }

